/**
 * Composite Readings — what a composite placement or aspect MEANS for the two
 * people in the relationship: behavior, feelings, fights, the trap, the move.
 *
 * NO ANATOMY: these never explain what a planet, sign or aspect is. The UI
 * heading already names the placement. Do not add definitions here.
 *
 * DUPLICATED verbatim in align-web/src/lib/compositeReadings.ts and
 * align-app/src/services/compositeReadings.ts — keep both in sync.
 */

const PLACEMENT_READINGS: Record<string, Record<string, string>> = {
  Sun: {
    Aries: "You two exist to start things. The relationship came alive the week one of you said 'let's just do it' and the other was already booking it. In public you look like a team that races, and privately you both keep a tally of who won the last argument, the last game night, the last decision about where to eat. When nothing new is on the calendar, you pick fights just to feel the old charge. The trap: mistaking friction for aliveness. The move: put one shared goal with a date on it on the fridge every season, and aim the competition there.",
    Taurus: "The two of you are building something you can touch: a home, a savings account, a routine that works. Friends call you steady, and you quietly take pride in being the couple whose plans don't fall apart. You both measure love in what stays, like the same booth at the same restaurant and the same Friday order. Change feels like a threat to the whole project, so a job offer in another city turns into weeks of silent resistance. The trap: calling stubbornness loyalty. The move: once a year, each of you names one thing you're scared to change, and you change it together.",
    Gemini: "You two are together to keep each other interested. The relationship runs on conversation: voice notes, half-finished debates, a group chat where you finish each other's jokes before anyone else can. Out in public you come across as the fun pair who knows a little about everyone. Underneath, you both get restless the moment things go quiet, and you fill the silence with plans, podcasts and other people. The trap: talking about everything except what's actually wrong between you. The move: one walk a week with phones left at home and a single rule, which is that the first topic is the hard one.",
    Cancer: "The whole point of you two is making a place where nobody has to perform. You built a home before you built a public image, and you both feel proudest when someone walks in and relaxes on your couch. You feed people, remember birthdays, and quietly adopt the friend who's going through a divorce. The downside shows up when the outside world asks for more of you: you retreat inward and treat invitations like intrusions. The trap: becoming a fortress that slowly shrinks to two people and a television. The move: say yes to one gathering a month outside your own walls, together.",
    Leo: "You two want to be seen, and honestly, people do look. The relationship shines brightest with an audience: the wedding toast, the anniversary post, the dinner party where you tell your origin story as a double act. Pride runs the show, and neither of you forgives being embarrassed by the other in front of friends. When the applause stops, one of you starts wondering whether the other still admires them. The trap: performing happiness online while starving for private praise at home. The move: tell each other one specific thing you're proud of, face to face, before you ever post it.",
    Virgo: "The two of you are together to make each other's lives work better. You fix things: the budget spreadsheet, the broken cabinet hinge, the other person's posture, the plan for their career. Friends call you the competent couple, the ones who actually show up with the right tools. The shadow side is that help slides into correction, and one of you starts feeling like a project under review. You both keep a quiet list of what the other hasn't improved yet. The trap: love that sounds like an audit. The move: for every fix you suggest this week, name one thing about each other you wouldn't change at all.",
    Libra: "You two are a partnership first and two individuals second, and everyone around you feels it. You decide things as a unit, host beautifully, and rarely let friends see you disagree. The relationship takes pride in being fair, which means you'll spend forty minutes negotiating whose turn it is to pick the film. Resentment doesn't explode between you; it gets politely filed away. The trap: keeping the peace so well that neither of you knows what the other actually wants anymore. The move: once a week, each of you makes one decision alone, and the other accepts it without edits.",
    Scorpio: "The two of you are together to change each other, whether you signed up for that or not. This relationship doesn't stay on the surface; within months you knew each other's worst memories, passwords and the full names of every ex. Outsiders find you private, a little intimidating, hard to read. You guard the relationship like a secret, and broken loyalty is the one thing neither of you forgives. The trap: running small tests to prove the bond still holds, like a delayed reply or a casual mention of an old flame. The move: stop testing, and ask the direct question you've been circling for weeks.",
    Sagittarius: "You two are together to go further than either of you would alone. The best version of this relationship has a passport stamp, a half-baked plan to move abroad, and a philosophy argument at 1 a.m. that nobody wins. People describe you as the couple always coming back from somewhere. The problem is ordinary Tuesdays: when life turns routine, one of you starts browsing flights and the other takes it personally. The trap: treating commitment and freedom as opposites and fighting over which one wins. The move: book the next adventure together before either of you feels trapped enough to go without the other.",
    Capricorn: "The two of you are building an empire, even if right now it's a mortgage and a five-year plan. This relationship takes its reputation seriously; you're the couple people ask for advice, the ones who look like they have it handled. You bond over goals, deadlines and proving the doubters wrong. Tenderness gets scheduled for after the big project, and the big project never ends. The trap: turning into business partners who share a bed and a calendar. The move: block one evening a week where logistics are banned, with no bills, no plans and no work talk, and protect it like a client meeting.",
    Aquarius: "You two are together to do it your own way, and you're proud that nobody quite understands your setup. Separate bedrooms, an odd schedule, a friendship that became something else without ever getting a label: whatever the details, friends see you as the couple with the unusual arrangement. You both value independence so much that asking for closeness feels like breaking the rules you wrote. The trap: staying so reasonable and detached that one of you gets lonely inside the relationship and never says it. The move: admit one plain, ordinary need this month, like 'I missed you today,' without explaining or justifying it.",
    Pisces: "The two of you are together for something that's hard to explain at parties. The relationship feels fated, a little unreal, and you both protect that feeling fiercely. You rescue each other, forgive fast, and blur where one person ends and the other begins. Outsiders sometimes worry you've disappeared into each other. Hard facts, like the unpaid bill or the unspoken resentment, get softened until they're invisible, then surface all at once. The trap: loving the dream of the relationship more than the two real people in it. The move: once a month, sit down and say three blunt truths out loud, including the unromantic ones.",
  },
  Moon: {
    Aries: "You two feel things fast and loud, and it's over before dinner goes cold. A snapped comment in the car becomes a full argument by the second traffic light, then someone cracks a joke and you're fine. Home is lively, not calm; you both get twitchy when an evening is too quiet. What makes you feel safe is honesty delivered instantly, even when it stings. The trap: forgetting that a fight ending fast isn't the same as the hurt healing. The move: after every blowup, circle back the next morning and ask, 'Is anything still sore from last night?'",
    Taurus: "Between you, comfort is physical: the same blanket, the same takeout order, feet on laps during the same show. You feel safe when life is predictable, and you both get strangely upset when someone rearranges the kitchen. Fights are slow to start and slower to finish, because one of you digs in and simply stops moving. Food settles more arguments here than words do. The trap: burying real problems under routine because the couch is too comfortable to leave. The move: when one of you goes stubborn and silent, set a time within two days to talk it through, and bring snacks.",
    Gemini: "You two process feelings by talking them to death, then texting about them from separate rooms. Home is noisy with ideas, open tabs and half-read books, and you feel safest when the conversation never stops. When something actually hurts, one of you gets clever instead of honest, and the other answers with a sharper line. Fights turn into debates about wording. The trap: analyzing a feeling so thoroughly that neither of you ever just feels it. The move: in your next argument, drop the reasoning and use one sentence only, 'I feel ___ because ___,' then stop talking and listen.",
    Cancer: "The two of you take care of each other the way family should and often doesn't. Home is the center of everything: soup when someone's sick, the favorite mug washed and waiting. You both remember every hurt, and an old wound from year one still comes up during a fight about the dishes. Moods fill the whole house, and one of you reads the other's silence from a room away. The trap: sulking and waiting to be rescued instead of saying what you need. The move: when you're hurt, say it straight within the hour, 'I need you to come sit with me,' and let that be enough.",
    Leo: "You two need to feel adored at home, not just in public. Grand gestures matter here: the surprise party, the dramatic apology, the 'you're the best thing that ever happened to me' said in front of friends. When one of you feels overlooked, the hurt comes out as a performance, a slammed cupboard or a wounded speech. Fights are about dignity more than the actual issue. The trap: both of you waiting for the other to make the first warm move while pride stretches the standoff across days. The move: be the one who apologizes first this time, and do it with real warmth, not a grudging mumble.",
    Virgo: "Between you, care looks like usefulness. You show love by fixing the leaky tap, packing the other's lunch, remembering the dentist appointment. You feel safe when the house is in order, and chaos, like a messy counter or an unpaid bill, spikes both your anxiety faster than you admit. Fights start small and precise: 'you always leave the towel there.' Underneath, the real complaint is 'I don't feel appreciated.' The trap: criticizing details because naming the need feels too exposing. The move: next time you're about to point out a small mistake, say the bigger thing instead: 'I'm stressed and I need help.'",
    Libra: "You two need peace at home so badly that you'll swallow a feeling to keep dinner pleasant. The house is pretty, the evenings civil, and outsiders assume you never fight. What actually happens is quiet accommodation: one of you says 'whatever you want' and means 'please read my mind.' Resentment builds in polite increments until a tiny thing sets off an oddly icy exchange over the dishwasher. The trap: confusing no conflict with no problems. The move: agree that either of you can call an 'honest ten minutes' at any time, where you say the unpleasant thing and the other doesn't smooth it over.",
    Scorpio: "Feelings between you run deep and stay hidden from everyone else. You bond through what you tell no one, and home is where the masks come off completely. Jealousy isn't a phase here; one of you notices every new name in the other's phone and says nothing. When hurt, you both withdraw and calculate rather than cry. Make-ups are intense and physical, which makes it easy to skip the actual conversation. The trap: keeping emotional secrets as protection and calling it privacy. The move: pick one fear about this relationship you've never told your partner, and say it this week, plainly, without softening it.",
    Sagittarius: "You two feel better the moment you're out the door. Comfort means a road trip, a new restaurant, a spontaneous weekend away, not a quiet night in. When something heavy comes up, one of you cracks a joke or suggests a hike, and the feeling gets left behind at the trailhead. Home can feel like a waiting room between adventures. Fights are blunt, even preachy, but you rarely hold grudges. The trap: outrunning sadness together until one of you crashes alone. The move: when a hard feeling shows up, stay in the same room for one full evening and let it be heavy before you plan any escape.",
    Capricorn: "The two of you handle feelings like responsibilities, something to manage rather than wallow in. When one of you is hurting, the other offers a plan before a hug. Home is orderly and run on duty: bills paid, family obligations met, nobody falling apart in public. You both feel safest when the future is secured, and money stress hits you harder than you let on. Fights go cold rather than hot. The trap: being so competent at coping that neither of you ever gets comforted. The move: once a week, ask 'what was hard today?' and answer each other without fixing anything.",
    Aquarius: "You two give each other a lot of space, and most days that feels like respect. You feel safe when neither of you is clingy, when you can retreat to separate rooms, friends and hobbies without explaining. But when real emotion shows up, you both reach for distance: reasoning, humor, a sudden fascination with something online. Fights sound calm and logical while someone is quietly devastated. The trap: treating vulnerability as neediness until closeness gets rationed. The move: when one of you says 'I'm fine' in that flat voice, the other is allowed, even required, to sit down and ask again.",
    Pisces: "Between you two, moods travel without words. One of you walks in sad and the other is suddenly sad too, without knowing why. Home is soft and dreamy: candles, music, long lazy mornings. Hurt rarely gets named; it drifts into hints, sighs and sudden tears over a film. Both of you dodge hard conversations by forgiving before anything is actually resolved. The trap: absorbing each other's feelings so completely that nobody can tell whose problem it is. The move: before comforting each other, ask one clear question, 'Is this mine, yours, or ours?', and wait for the answer.",
  },
  Ascendant: {
    Aries: "People notice you two the second you walk in, usually because one of you is already mid-story and the other is interrupting. It started fast: a bold first move, a first date that turned into a whole weekend. Friends see you as the couple that dares each other into things. Strangers sometimes mistake your banter for an actual fight. The trap: letting that combative public show become how you talk in private too, until the edge stops being playful. The move: at your next dinner with friends, back each other up out loud once, on purpose, and notice how different it feels.",
    Taurus: "From the outside you two look solid, the couple that seems to have been together longer than you have. It started slowly: a friendship, repeated coffees, one of you waiting patiently until the other caught up. People find you calming to be around, the pair with the nice home and the good wine. Outsiders assume nothing ever shakes you. The trap: that steady image makes it hard to admit when you're stuck, so friends are shocked when trouble finally surfaces. The move: next time things are hard, tell one trusted friend the truth instead of keeping up the calm front.",
    Gemini: "People meet you two and think you're best friends first, a couple second. It started with talking: a message thread that ran for hours, a joke that kept going for weeks. You're quick together, bouncing between topics and finishing each other's sentences in a way that's charming for about ten minutes. Some friends aren't sure how serious you are, because you keep it light in public. The trap: staying so breezy that outsiders, and sometimes you two, never see the real depth of the commitment. The move: say something sincere about each other in front of people you trust, without turning it into a joke.",
    Cancer: "The two of you come across as warm but guarded, the couple who feels like home to your friends yet takes ages to open up to strangers. It started with care: one of you looked after the other through something hard. People describe you as protective of each other, sometimes too protective. At parties you drift together into a corner. The trap: a closed-circle vibe that makes new people feel like outsiders and slowly thins your social life. The move: at the next gathering, split up for an hour, then compare notes on who you met during the car ride home.",
    Leo: "You two make an entrance, and people remember it. It started with a spark others witnessed: the flirting at a party, the public declaration, the first photo that got everyone talking. Friends see you as the golden couple, generous hosts and loud laughers with a flair for drama. You both like looking good together, and you quietly care what people think of your relationship. The trap: managing the image so carefully that nobody, including you, knows how things actually are behind closed doors. The move: let one close friend see an unpolished moment, a real disagreement or a bad day, without spinning it.",
    Virgo: "People see you two as the practical, organized pair, the ones with the shared calendar and the dinner reservation already made. It began around something real: a job, a class, a volunteer shift, helping each other get something done. You come across as understated and reserved about affection in public. Friends trust your advice because you both notice details. The trap: looking so tidy and functional that people assume the romance is gone, and one of you starts believing it too. The move: hold hands in public, visibly, even when it feels unnecessary, and let people catch you flirting.",
    Libra: "The two of you look like a matched set: well dressed, polite, easy to invite anywhere. It started charmingly, with a proper date, good manners and a clear sense of being chosen. People describe you as the nice couple, the fair ones, the pair who never makes a scene. That reputation becomes something you protect, so you smile through dinners and then go silent and furious in the car. The trap: caring more about how the relationship looks than how it feels. The move: next time you're upset at a social event, say 'let's leave early' and have the real talk before the reputation takes over.",
    Scorpio: "People can't quite read you two, and that's the point. You walk in with an intensity that makes strangers curious and a little wary. It began with instant magnetism, a look held too long, and often a complicated situation neither of you talks about. Friends know very little about what really goes on between you. The trap: that sealed-off vibe makes people assume the worst or stop trying to get close to you as a couple. The move: invite another couple over and let them see your home, your jokes and your ordinary side, because secrecy isn't the same as intimacy.",
    Sagittarius: "You two come off as the fun, adventurous couple, always planning a trip and always up for one more drink. It started somewhere unexpected: while traveling, across a culture gap, or through a wild coincidence you love retelling. People find you open, funny and a bit loud. Friends sometimes wonder whether you'll actually settle down, because you both joke about commitment so casually. The trap: playing up the free-spirit image until one of you believes the other isn't serious. The move: say out loud, in front of people, that you're in this for the long haul, and let it stand without a punchline.",
    Capricorn: "People see you two as the serious, grown-up couple, even if you're young. It began as a slow build, often with an age or status gap that others took a while to accept. You come across as capable and slightly formal in public, the pair who shows up on time with a proper gift. Friends respect you but don't always feel close to you. The trap: seeming so composed that no one guesses you need support, including your own families. The move: let people see you laugh at each other's ridiculous side, and ask for help once before you're desperate.",
    Aquarius: "You two strike people as unusual, the couple that doesn't follow the normal script. Whether it started online, through a friend group, or in some odd way you still have to explain at weddings, the story never sounds typical. You come across as friendly and independent, more like teammates than lovebirds. People sometimes can't tell you're together until someone tells them. The trap: guarding your independence in public so well that your partner feels like one friend among many. The move: at the next group event, stand next to each other longer than feels necessary and make it obvious who you're going home with.",
    Pisces: "People feel something soft and a bit mysterious around you two. It began in a dreamlike way: a chance meeting, a sense of already knowing each other, sometimes an overlap that was messy at first. You come across as gentle, easy to talk to, and hard to pin down. Friends bring you their problems, and you both absorb them. The trap: letting everyone else's version of your story define you, because neither of you pushes back on how people see you. The move: agree on your own clear answer to 'so what are you two?' and say it the same way every time.",
  },
  Mercury: {
    Aries: "You two talk like you're both racing to the finish line, and half your sentences get finished by the wrong person. Decisions happen in thirty seconds, which is great for picking a restaurant and terrible for picking a lease. Arguments flare hot, somebody says the sharp thing first, and ten minutes later you're both acting like it never happened. Outsiders think you're fighting when you're just talking. The trap: the blunt line that lands and never gets taken back, so it quietly piles up. The move: when one of you says something cutting, the other says 'rewind' and the speaker has to say it again, slower.",
    Taurus: "Between you, conversations move at walking pace and nobody gets rushed into an answer. You can spend three weeks deciding on a couch and both feel good about it. Your best talks happen over food, and your inside jokes are the same five phrases repeated for years. The problem is that once either of you has said 'I've made up my mind,' the discussion is over, and the other one stops trying. The trap: the same argument about money or the family visit on repeat, word for word, because neither of you budges an inch. The move: before you dig in, each of you names one thing you'd trade to get what you want.",
    Gemini: "The two of you text all day about nothing and everything, and your phones hold a thousand unfinished conversations. You jump from a work drama to a documentary to a rumor about a friend in one breath, and it's the most fun either of you has talking to anyone. But you're so busy being clever that the one serious topic keeps getting dodged with a joke. People at parties notice you narrating the room to each other. The trap: talking about everything except the thing that's actually bothering one of you. The move: once a week, put the phones face down and finish exactly one hard conversation before anyone changes the subject.",
    Cancer: "You two don't really hear words so much as tone, and a clipped 'fine' in a text can ruin an afternoon. Both of you remember exactly what was said during the worst fight, down to the phrasing, and it comes back out months later. Your real talks happen in the kitchen or in bed with the lights off, never in public. You also talk about your families more than either of you admits. The trap: replying to how something sounded instead of what was meant, then sulking about it. The move: when a message stings, ask 'did you mean that the way I heard it?' before you react.",
    Leo: "You two are a double act, and your best stories get better every time you tell them at dinner. Each of you wants the other to laugh hardest at your jokes, and it quietly stings when that laugh goes to somebody else. In arguments, the real wound is rarely the topic; it's feeling talked down to. You both hate admitting that the other person's idea was the good one. The trap: retelling a private fight to friends as a funny bit, turning your partner into the punchline. The move: give credit out loud, in front of people, the next time the other one is right.",
    Virgo: "Between you, love sounds like corrections: 'you're holding the knife wrong,' 'that's not what the email said.' You run your life off shared lists and group calendars, and you're genuinely good at solving problems together. But the steady stream of small fixes lands as criticism, and one of you has started editing yourself before speaking. You'd both rather analyze a feeling than just have it. The trap: turning every conversation into a performance review, so the compliments get buried under the notes. The move: for every fix you point out, name one thing the other did right that day, specifically and without a 'but.'",
    Libra: "You two are so polite with each other that outsiders assume you never fight. The truth is that 'I don't mind, what do you want?' gets passed back and forth until dinner is at nine and nobody chose anything. You both soften every hard sentence until the actual point disappears. Resentment shows up later as a sigh or a joke with an edge. You're brilliant at talking other couples through their problems and terrible at naming your own. The trap: agreeing out loud and disagreeing in private. The move: pick one decision a week where one of you has to say a flat 'no' and the other has to accept it without negotiating.",
    Scorpio: "Nothing gets said casually between you; every text gets read three times for what's underneath. You two can have an entire argument through a pause on the phone. Both of you notice when a story has changed slightly since the last time it was told, and neither of you lets it slide. Your conversations go deeper than anything either of you has had before, but they can feel like a cross-examination. The trap: holding information back as leverage, then acting wounded when the other one does the same. The move: agree on one topic that is fully open, where any question gets a straight answer the first time it's asked.",
    Sagittarius: "You two talk big: road trips, moving countries, the meaning of life at 1 a.m. on the balcony. Conversations turn into debates, and debates turn into laughing at how seriously you both took it. The problem is that 'we should totally do that' comes out of your mouths weekly and lands on the calendar almost never. One of you also says the brutally honest thing and then calls the other oversensitive for flinching. The trap: grand promises that turn into a running joke, and bluntness used as a license. The move: every plan you get excited about gets a date and a name attached before the conversation ends.",
    Capricorn: "The two of you talk like co-founders, and your most intimate conversations sometimes sound like budget meetings. You're excellent at five-year plans, dividing up errands, and saying exactly what needs to happen next. Your humor is dry enough that friends can't always tell when you're joking. The catch is that feelings get scheduled for later, and later rarely arrives. When something hurts, one of you states the facts in a flat voice and the other hears coldness. The trap: solving the problem so efficiently that nobody asks how the other one feels about it. The move: before any practical decision, each of you says one sentence that starts with 'I feel.'",
    Aquarius: "You two argue about ideas for fun and can spend an entire dinner defending opposite sides of something neither of you cares about. Your inside jokes are strange enough that friends have stopped asking. But when the topic gets personal, you both go analytical and start discussing the relationship like it belongs to someone else. One of you says 'I'm just being logical' right when the other needed warmth. The trap: winning the argument and losing the person across the table. The move: when a talk gets heated, stop debating and ask 'what do you need from me right now?' then actually do that thing.",
    Pisces: "Between you, a lot gets communicated without words: a look across the room, a song sent at midnight, a meme that says what neither of you could. When it works, it feels like you share one mind. When it doesn't, one of you is hurt that the other didn't just know. Plans stay vague, texts go unanswered for hours, and details slip through the cracks of both your memories. The trap: expecting to be read perfectly and punishing the other quietly when it doesn't happen. The move: say the need in plain words, even if it feels unromantic to spell it out.",
  },
  Venus: {
    Aries: "You two fell for each other fast, and you still flirt like it's a race. Affection between you comes as action: showing up unannounced, grabbing a hand across the table, booking the trip before checking the bank balance. Money goes out quickly and nobody wants to be the one who says slow down. Romance dies for you the minute it gets predictable, so a routine Friday night feels like a small insult. The trap: chasing new thrills instead of tending what you already have. The move: once a week, do something slow on purpose and stay with it until it stops feeling boring.",
    Taurus: "The two of you show love with things you can touch: the good sheets, the takeout order memorized, the hand resting on a thigh during a movie. Your home looks like two people who argued seriously about a couch and both won. Money is comfort between you, so you spend on quality and then quietly resent the credit card statement together. Outsiders call you settled; you call it finally feeling safe. The trap: letting comfort replace courtship until you're roommates with great taste. The move: once a month, put on real clothes, leave the house, and flirt like you're still trying to win each other.",
    Gemini: "You two fell for each other's minds first, and the texting never stopped. Love between you sounds like a running commentary: memes at midnight, voice notes, a joke that started three years ago and still gets a laugh. Money disappears on small, scattered things like books, apps, and last-minute tickets, and nobody remembers where it went. You get bored in silence faster than you get bored with each other. The trap: talking about feelings so cleverly that neither of you actually says one. The move: put the phones in another room once a week and say one plain sentence, no jokes: 'Here's what I love about you right now.'",
    Cancer: "The two of you love by feeding, fussing, and remembering. One of you knows exactly how the other takes their tea on a bad day, and that detail matters more than any gift. Your money goes into the nest: the kitchen, the family visits, the savings account with a vague 'someday' label. You both keep a private ledger of who cared for whom, and hurt lands hard when care goes unnoticed. The trap: sulking when affection isn't returned instead of asking for it. The move: when you feel unloved, say the exact thing you need, like 'sit with me' or 'make dinner tonight,' before the resentment sets.",
    Leo: "You two love out loud. There's the big birthday, the public post, the outfit chosen so you look good as a pair walking in. Friends notice the chemistry, and honestly, you both like that they notice. Money goes to experiences worth showing off, and the budget loses every time. Underneath the show, each of you needs to hear you're still the favorite, and one distracted evening feels like being demoted. The trap: performing romance for an audience while starving for private attention. The move: once a week, do something loving that nobody else will ever see or hear about, and never mention it later.",
    Virgo: "You two show love by fixing things. One of you refills the prescription, the other rewrites the resume, and both of you call it romance. Money is handled carefully, with spreadsheets, price comparisons, and a quiet pride in not wasting, so a splurge triggers a real conversation. Your affection lives in the details, which means your criticism does too: a dishwasher loaded wrong feels like a comment on the whole relationship. The trap: correcting each other so often that praise becomes rare and suspicious. The move: for every note you give, say two specific things you admire, out loud, the same day.",
    Libra: "The two of you are good at being a couple: the dinner parties, the shared taste, the photos where everyone looks relaxed. You love through beauty and fairness, splitting the bill evenly, taking turns choosing the restaurant, making the apartment feel like a hotel you'd pay for. Conflict feels ugly to you both, so irritation gets smoothed over with a compliment. Friends think you never fight; really, you just never finish one. The trap: keeping the peace until someone quietly checks out. The move: hold a monthly honest talk where each of you names one thing that bugs you, and nobody is allowed to be charming about it.",
    Scorpio: "You two don't love halfway. Once you picked each other, the rest of the world got smaller, and neither of you pretends otherwise. Affection is private and intense: the long look across a crowded room, knowing each other's passwords, secrets no friend will ever hear. Money gets tangled early and turns into a trust issue the moment one of you spends without saying. Jealousy shows up as questions that sound casual and aren't. The trap: testing loyalty instead of asking for reassurance. The move: when suspicion rises, say 'I'm feeling insecure' before you check anything or ask a loaded question.",
    Sagittarius: "The two of you fall in love again every time you leave town. Your best memories have airports in them, and your worst fights happen after too many ordinary weeks at home. Affection comes as laughter and big plans, like 'let's move abroad' or 'let's quit and start something,' and money follows those plans without much looking back. You both hate being told what to do, so jealousy gets played as cool indifference. The trap: treating commitment like a cage and keeping one foot out the door. The move: plan the next adventure together out loud, with a date and a budget, so freedom becomes something you share.",
    Capricorn: "You two treat love as something built, not something felt on a whim. Affection shows up as reliability: the paid bill, the ride to the airport at 5 a.m., the long-term plan with an actual timeline. Money is serious between you, and big purchases get debated like business deals. Outsiders call you a power couple and wonder whether you have fun; sometimes you wonder too. Tenderness gets postponed until after the deadline, the promotion, the house. The trap: proving love through achievement while nobody says it. The move: put a non-negotiable date night on the calendar and treat skipping it like missing a work meeting.",
    Aquarius: "The two of you built a relationship that doesn't look like anyone else's, and you're a little proud of it. You're friends first, the kind who debate ideas at dinner and keep separate hobbies without drama. Money gets split in odd, fair-minded ways that confuse your parents. Affection is real but understated; a link sent at exactly the right moment counts as romance. The trap: so much independence that one of you starts feeling like a roommate with benefits. The move: once a week, drop the cool distance and ask directly, 'Do you feel close to me right now?' and then answer honestly.",
    Pisces: "You two love like a movie soundtrack: the song that became yours, the handwritten notes, the feeling of being understood without explaining. Both of you give until it hurts and then hide how tired you are. Money slips through your fingers on gifts, rescues, and friends who needed a loan. You see the best in each other so clearly that the real person occasionally feels like a letdown. The trap: forgiving everything silently and drifting into quiet martyrdom. The move: say no to each other at least once a week about something small, and notice that the love survives it.",
  },
  Mars: {
    Aries: "You two fight fast and loud, and the argument is usually over before the neighbors get curious. Neither of you backs down first, so small things like who drives or which exit to take turn into a contest in under a minute. The chemistry is immediate and physical; making up often happens in the bedroom before the issue is actually settled. You push each other to start things: the gym routine, the business idea, the move. The trap: winning the argument and losing the point. The move: when voices rise, one of you calls a ten-minute walk, then you come back and each name what you actually wanted.",
    Taurus: "The two of you are slow to anger and almost impossible to move once you get there. Fights between you are standoffs: nobody yells, nobody budges, and the same disagreement about money or the in-laws comes back for years. Physical chemistry is steady and sensual, with long mornings and touch that doesn't need an occasion. When you decide on a goal together, you outlast everyone. The trap: stubborn silence that turns one argument into a month-long cold war. The move: any standoff older than three days gets a sit-down where each of you offers one real concession before dinner.",
    Gemini: "You two fight with words, and both of you are good at it. Arguments jump topics: it starts with the dishes and ends with something said at a party two years ago. Texts get sharp, sarcasm lands as a weapon, and whoever's quicker wins the round but not the peace. Attraction runs through banter; flirting is foreplay, and a good debate often ends up somewhere physical. The trap: arguing about everything except the one thing that's actually wrong. The move: when a fight scatters, stop and each finish this sentence in one line: 'What I'm really upset about is...'",
    Cancer: "The two of you rarely fight head-on. Anger comes out sideways: slammed cupboards, a clipped 'I'm fine,' a pointed reminder of who forgot the anniversary. Both of you protect yourselves by pulling back, so the real argument happens in your heads while the room stays quiet. When someone threatens your family or your home, though, you turn fierce as a unit. Sex is tied to feeling safe, and after a tense week desire shuts off completely. The trap: sulking until the other one guesses. The move: say the anger plainly within a day, starting with 'I felt hurt when,' and let the other respond before anyone retreats.",
    Leo: "You two fight like it's a stage play, and pride writes the script. Nobody wants to apologize first, because apologizing feels like losing face, so both of you hold out for a grand gesture. The chemistry is loud and flattering: you each want to feel desired, chosen, looked at. Public embarrassment is the one thing neither of you forgives easily, and a joke at the other's expense in front of friends gets replayed for weeks. The trap: waiting for the other to crawl back. The move: make the first apology small and fast, 'I was wrong about that part,' and watch how quickly the ice breaks.",
    Virgo: "The two of you fight about details, and the details are never really the point. A towel on the floor becomes a lecture, and the lecture becomes a verdict on who works harder. You both notice everything, so criticism slips out before kindness does. Physical chemistry builds slowly and depends on stress levels; an overflowing inbox kills desire faster than any argument. You're a strong team on projects, especially fixing something broken. The trap: nitpicking as a substitute for saying 'I'm overwhelmed.' The move: before correcting anything, ask 'Are you stressed?' and deal with that first.",
    Libra: "You two hate fighting so much that you fight about how you fight. One of you wants to talk it out now, the other wants to wait until it's calmer, and meanwhile the resentment grows politely. Anger comes wrapped in fairness: 'I'm just saying it's not balanced.' Attraction is tied to feeling wanted and attractive, and one sloppy, careless week cools things fast. Decisions stall because nobody wants to be the pushy one. The trap: passive-aggressive peace that nobody actually believes. The move: agree that either of you can say 'I disagree' without it being a crisis, and then actually pick something.",
    Scorpio: "The two of you don't argue; you go to war, quietly. Fights run deep, touch old wounds, and nobody forgets what was said. Both of you know exactly where the other's soft spots are, and in a bad moment you use them. The physical chemistry is intense and a little obsessive, and sex is where trust gets proven or broken. Power struggles show up over money, phones, and who controls the plans. The trap: revenge through withdrawal, withholding touch, attention, or information. The move: agree on one off-limits topic neither of you ever uses as ammunition, and keep that promise even when furious.",
    Sagittarius: "You two blow up fast, say something blunt, and are laughing about it an hour later. Honesty is the weapon of choice, and neither of you softens the delivery. Arguments turn into debates about principles like politics, religion, or how to raise kids, and the original issue gets lost. Chemistry is playful and spontaneous; hotel rooms and road trips light you both up. Restlessness is your biggest trigger: when life feels stuck, you pick fights just to feel something move. The trap: tactless truths that leave bruises you don't notice. The move: after every blowup, ask 'Did I say something that stuck?' and actually listen.",
    Capricorn: "The two of you fight like executives in a budget meeting: controlled, strategic, and cold. Anger shows up as criticism about responsibility, meaning who dropped the ball and who isn't pulling their weight. Neither of you likes losing control, so emotion gets bottled until it cracks at the worst time. Physical chemistry is slow-burning and surprisingly strong once work is off your minds. Together you're relentless about goals and outwork everyone around you. The trap: treating each other like employees who underperformed. The move: once a week, drop the scorecard and ask 'What do you need from me that isn't a task?'",
    Aquarius: "You two fight by detaching. When things heat up, one of you goes cool and logical, and the other finds that more infuriating than yelling. Arguments become debates about fairness, and whoever sounds more reasonable believes they won. Chemistry is unconventional: you like experiments, surprises, and doing things your friends would never guess. You both rebel against feeling controlled, so a simple request lands like a rule. The trap: winning on logic while the other feels dismissed. The move: before arguing the point, say back what the other person is feeling, in their words, until they agree you got it right.",
    Pisces: "The two of you avoid direct conflict until it leaks out as guilt, tears, or a sudden cold shoulder. Nobody says 'I'm angry'; they say 'I'm just tired.' Resentment builds quietly, then one of you disappears into work, a phone, or a drink for the evening. Chemistry is dreamy and emotional: sex feels best when you both feel understood, and it vanishes when you don't. Drive between you rises and falls with mood. The trap: playing the victim so neither of you has to own the anger. The move: practice saying 'I'm mad about this' in a normal voice, until it becomes a normal thing to say.",
  },
  Jupiter: {
    Aries: "This relationship made both of you braver. Together you sign up for the marathon, quit the job, book the one-way ticket, and dare each other into things neither of you would try alone. You're generous in bursts, throwing money or time at a big gesture on impulse. Friends say you two are a bad influence on each other in the best way. The overdoing shows up as starting ten things and finishing two, and as egging each other on past the point of sense. The trap: chasing the next rush because ordinary weeks feel like failure. The move: before each new adventure, finish or formally drop one you already started.",
    Taurus: "Between you, growth looks like comfort that compounds: a better kitchen, a nicer mattress, a savings account that finally has something in it. You two are generous with food, gifts, and hosting, and your home is where friends end up the morning after the party. You believe in building something real and slow. The overdoing is in pleasure itself: the takeout habit, the second bottle, the 'we deserve it' purchases that quietly stack up. The trap: getting so cozy that nothing new ever gets in, and your waistlines and credit cards show it. The move: trade one indulgence a month for a new experience you've never tried together.",
    Gemini: "You two expand each other's minds constantly: books passed back and forth, podcasts sent mid-episode, weekend trips to places you read about at midnight. Together you're curious about everyone and can talk to anyone at a wedding. Your circle got bigger because of this relationship. The overdoing is in commitments: saying yes to three events on one Saturday and running late to all of them. You also collect half-learned hobbies like souvenirs. The trap: skimming across a hundred interests and never going deep enough in one to be changed by it. The move: pick one shared skill this year and stick with it past the boring middle.",
    Cancer: "This relationship grows both of you through belonging. You two open your home, feed people, and keep a door open for friends going through breakups. Family matters a great deal here, whether you're building one or quietly healing the one you came from. You take care of each other generously when one of you is sick or grieving. The overdoing is in taking in too many people's problems and letting relatives set up camp in your life. The trap: mothering everyone, including each other, until nobody feels like an adult. The move: agree on a limit for how often family and friends get your weekends, and hold it together.",
    Leo: "Together you two get bigger, louder, and more confident, and people notice when you walk in. This relationship pushed at least one of you to finally chase the creative thing or take the stage. You celebrate each other lavishly: surprise parties, public toasts, gifts that make a statement. The overdoing is in the performance: spending to look like the couple everyone envies, and needing an audience for your happiness. When one of you gets the spotlight, the other can feel it tighten. The trap: living for the photos and the applause instead of what happens after the guests go home. The move: plan one generous thing for each other that nobody else will ever see or hear about.",
    Virgo: "You two grow by getting better at life: healthier routines, cleaner finances, a household that actually runs. Together you've fixed habits neither of you could fix alone. Your generosity is practical; you show up with soup, you do the taxes, you help friends move. You believe in effort and improvement. The overdoing shows up as endless self-improvement projects that turn the relationship into a program. There's always another diet, another system, another thing to optimize. The trap: treating each other like a work in progress and never feeling like enough. The move: schedule one day a month with no goals, no tracking, and no fixing anything.",
    Libra: "This relationship made both of you more graceful with people. Together you two are the couple who gets invited to everything, smooths over tension at family dinners, and remembers everyone's birthday. You grow through partnership itself, learning to share decisions and see the other side. You're generous with compliments and hospitality. The overdoing is in pleasing: accepting every invitation, splitting yourselves between everyone's needs, and spending money to keep up appearances. The trap: being so good at keeping the peace that neither of you ever says what you want. The move: say no together to one social obligation a month and spend that time alone as a pair.",
    Scorpio: "The two of you grow through depth, and this relationship has dragged things into the light that both of you had hidden for years. Together you've survived something that would have ended most couples, and it made you closer. You're generous in a private, intense way: total loyalty, and a willingness to go to war for each other. Shared money and resources tend to multiply here. The overdoing is in intensity itself, turning ordinary disagreements into all-or-nothing crises. The trap: needing a crisis to feel close. The move: when things are calm, deliberately build closeness on purpose, like a standing night where you talk about anything except problems.",
    Sagittarius: "You two are at your best on the road, and your relationship keeps a list of countries, campsites, and odd little towns. Together you've questioned the beliefs you were raised with and built your own. You laugh a lot, and you're generous to a fault with strangers, tips, and second chances. The overdoing is in restlessness and promises: booking the trip you can't afford, committing to plans you both forget. When home life gets dull, you both get itchy. The trap: running toward the next horizon instead of dealing with what's piling up at home. The move: every big trip gets paid for in cash first, and every return gets a week of dull, honest catching up.",
    Capricorn: "This relationship grows you both through ambition, and you've helped each other climb in ways that show up on paper: promotions, property, a business. Together you believe in earning things the hard way, and you're generous with advice, connections, and sensible gifts. Friends trust you two with their serious decisions. The overdoing is in work: fun keeps getting postponed until after the next milestone, and the milestones keep moving. The trap: building a great life on paper that you're both too busy to actually live in. The move: put one non-negotiable, completely unproductive weekend on the calendar every quarter and protect it like a deadline.",
    Aquarius: "The two of you grow by breaking the rules other couples follow. Together you've made up your own version of commitment, holidays, or living arrangements, and you don't apologize for it. Your friends are a wide, odd mix, and your home often becomes a gathering place for people who don't fit elsewhere. You're generous with causes and your community. The overdoing is in independence: so much freedom and so many outside projects that you forget to show up for each other. The trap: being so progressive about the relationship that you both avoid admitting you need more closeness. The move: keep one ordinary tradition that's just yours, and never skip it.",
    Pisces: "This relationship softened both of you and opened something spiritual or creative that neither of you had before. Together you're forgiving, deeply kind, and quick to rescue strays, friends in trouble, and lost causes. There's a sense that you two were meant to find each other. The overdoing is in faith and escape: believing things will work out while the bills pile up, or drifting into too much wine, too much screen time, too much fantasy. The trap: giving endlessly to people who drain you and calling it compassion. The move: agree on one practical anchor, like a monthly money check-in, that keeps the dream standing on solid ground.",
  },
  Saturn: {
    Aries: "The hard lesson for you two is patience with each other. Both of you are used to acting first and explaining later, and this relationship keeps punishing that. Every time one of you makes a big decision alone, trust takes months to rebuild. Your fights are rarely about the topic; they're about who got to decide. There's a quiet fear that slowing down means losing yourself. The trap: treating compromise like defeat, so you both keep winning battles and the relationship keeps losing. The move: make a hard rule that no decision over a set dollar amount or a big life change gets made without a 24-hour pause and a real conversation.",
    Taurus: "Between you, the test is money and security, and it's slow and heavy. You two argue less often than other couples but more stubbornly, and the same financial fight has been simmering for years. Both of you fear losing what you've built, so neither of you wants to risk the move that would actually improve it. Affection can start to feel like another obligation. The trap: holding on so tightly to stability that the relationship becomes a well-kept house nobody enjoys living in. The move: build a shared financial plan with actual numbers, then set aside a small fund that exists only for pleasure, no questions asked.",
    Gemini: "The two of you have to earn trust through words, and it doesn't come easily. Every broken promise, even 'I'll call you back,' gets filed away. At least one of you learned early that talking about feelings was dangerous, so hard conversations stall or turn into lectures. Crossed wires in texts cost you more than they should. The trap: going quiet on the important things while chatting about everything else, until the silence becomes a wall. The move: build one reliable ritual, like a weekly sit-down where each of you says one thing that's bothering you and the other only listens, and never skip it.",
    Cancer: "This relationship tests how safe you two can really make home. At least one of you carries old family weight, and it shows up in how you both handle closeness: guarded, careful, braced for rejection. Holidays with relatives are often where the real strain surfaces. There's a deep fear of being abandoned or ending up like your parents. The trap: protecting yourselves so carefully that neither of you ever lets the other all the way in. The move: build home on purpose, with your own rules about family visits, your own traditions, and a standing promise that no one leaves the house mid-fight.",
    Leo: "The test between you is whether you can love each other without an audience. At some point the applause fades, and both of you have to feel proud of this relationship when nobody's watching. One of you often feels unappreciated, and the other feels like nothing is ever enough. The fear is of being ordinary together. The trap: withholding praise because you're afraid it'll make the other one lazy or arrogant. The move: build a daily habit of saying one specific thing you admire about each other, out loud and in private, especially on the weeks it feels hardest to find.",
    Virgo: "For you two, the hard part is the daily grind of partnership: chores, schedules, health, and who does more. The ledger in both your heads is precise, and it's rarely even. Criticism comes easily, praise comes slowly, and one of you has started to feel like an employee. Health scares or work stress hit this relationship hard. The trap: turning love into a list of duties until you're both exhausted and resentful. The move: write down, together, the actual division of household labor, rebalance it fairly, then add one weekly act of care that isn't on anybody's list.",
    Libra: "The commitment test here is fairness, and it shows up in every contract, lease, and conversation about the future. You two take the promise itself seriously, sometimes more seriously than the romance. But one of you tends to carry more of the compromise, and the imbalance builds quietly until it breaks through. You both fear conflict because conflict feels like the beginning of the end. The trap: keeping the peace so long that resentment becomes the real third person in the room. The move: agree to renegotiate the relationship's terms out loud once a year, like a contract review, where nothing is off the table.",
    Scorpio: "The hardest lesson between you is trust, and it gets tested around jealousy, money, sex, or a secret that came out. You two don't do easy forgiveness. Both of you fear betrayal so deeply that you sometimes create the distance you're afraid of. Control creeps in quietly: checking phones, tracking spending, reading silence as guilt. The trap: waiting for proof the other will leave, and never getting the reassurance you both actually need. The move: build full transparency on the thing that scares you most, whether that's passwords, accounts, or past relationships, and then deliberately stop checking.",
    Sagittarius: "The test between you two is whether freedom and commitment can live in the same house. One of you often feels fenced in, the other feels like the flight risk is always one bad week away. You argue about beliefs, religion, where to live, or how to raise kids, and it runs deeper than you let on. There's a fear that settling down means giving up the life you wanted. The trap: keeping one foot out the door so neither of you fully commits. The move: sit down and write the shared beliefs your relationship stands on, then plan the adventures that fit inside them.",
    Capricorn: "You two are built for the long haul, and you both know it, which is exactly why the pressure is so heavy. The relationship runs on responsibility: kids, careers, mortgages, aging parents. Romance gets filed under 'later' and later never shows up. You both fear failing at this more than you fear being unhappy in it. The trap: becoming excellent business partners who haven't touched each other in weeks. The move: treat intimacy like any other commitment, with a scheduled night every week that's protected from work calls, errands, and the kids.",
    Aquarius: "The hard thing between you is closeness itself. You two value space, and at first that felt like maturity, but now distance is doing some of the damage. One of you gets cold and detached under stress; the other reads it as not caring. Friends or outside causes quietly take priority when things get uncomfortable at home. The fear is of losing your individuality inside the couple. The trap: calling emotional avoidance 'independence.' The move: build a rule that when one of you pulls away, you say out loud 'I need space for a few hours,' and then you come back and talk.",
    Pisces: "The test for you two is facing reality together. This relationship carries a lot of dreams, but also some sacrifice, and one of you often gives up more than the other notices. Hard truths get softened until they're no longer true, and problems get handled by hoping. The quiet fear is that looking at things clearly will end the magic. The trap: rescuing each other from consequences so the same crisis keeps coming back in a new form. The move: build one clear boundary around your weakest spot, whether that's money, drinking, or a draining family member, and hold it together even when it feels unkind.",
  },
  Uranus: {
    Aries: "You two bolt before you think, and half your best memories started with one of you saying 'let's just go' at 11 p.m. Neither of you asks permission, so plans get announced instead of discussed, and the other finds out about the new job or the haircut after it happens. That jolt keeps the attraction alive, but it also trains you both to act solo and apologize later. The trap: treating every 'can we talk first?' as a leash. The move: keep your wild starts, and add one rule you both obey, a ten-minute heads-up text before any big leap.",
    Taurus: "You two look steady from the outside, then one of you sells the couch, quits the gym membership, or moves the savings into something nobody else understands. Your shared money and your routines are where the surprises land, and the quiet one of you feels it in the stomach before saying a word. You both crave comfort and then get bored of it within weeks. The trap: shaking up the bank account to feel alive instead of shaking up the weekend. The move: set aside one fund that is allowed to be reckless, and leave the rent money boring on purpose.",
    Gemini: "You two talk in bursts, then vanish from each other's texts for a day, and neither of you calls it a problem. Your conversations jump across five topics in one car ride, and the best ideas show up mid-sentence and get forgotten by dinner. Outsiders find your banter confusing, and you like it that way. The cost is that the serious thing one of you tried to say got buried under a joke or a meme. The trap: keeping everything light so nobody gets pinned down. The move: when one of you says 'no, actually listen,' the phones go face down.",
    Cancer: "You two refuse to build the home your parents built, and the families notice. Holidays get skipped, the living arrangement looks odd to relatives, and your idea of cozy includes a lot of time in separate rooms. Closeness arrives in waves: a week of glued-together nesting, then one of you needs a night out alone with zero explanation. The partner left behind reads it as rejection and goes cold. The trap: calling emotional distance 'independence' when it's really avoidance. The move: say where you're going and why before you leave, then come back and actually sit on the same couch.",
    Leo: "You two can't stand a romance that looks like everyone else's, so your dates are odd, your milestones get celebrated in unconventional ways, and your photos never look like the couples on the feed. You flirt by provoking each other, and the spark lives in being surprised. When the novelty dips, one of you starts performing for an audience outside the relationship, a new crowd, a new project, somebody who laughs harder. The trap: chasing applause elsewhere because home got predictable. The move: take turns planning one genuinely strange date a month, and let the other be the only audience that counts.",
    Virgo: "You two rewrite your daily routine every few months, new sleep schedule, new diet, new app for the chores, and abandon it just as fast. Work hours clash, someone is always pulling a strange shift or freelancing, and the dishes become a symbol of who is being unfair. You're brilliant at fixing each other's problems in clever ways and awful at doing the same boring thing twice. The trap: nitpicking the other's system instead of admitting neither of you likes systems. The move: agree on three non-negotiable chores with names attached, and let everything else stay experimental.",
    Libra: "You two wrote your own rules for this relationship, and at some point someone at a dinner party asked 'wait, so what are you?' You need space inside the partnership, separate friends, separate trips, and you both get jumpy when things feel too couple-y. Fairness matters more than tradition, but the rules keep changing without anyone announcing it. One of you is always on a different page of the agreement. The trap: renegotiating the whole deal every time one of you feels restless. The move: write the agreement down, literally, and review it together twice a year instead of in the middle of a fight.",
    Scorpio: "You two go from total closeness to sudden cold, and the switch flips without warning. The bedroom is where you experiment and where things change fastest, and one of you tends to drop a secret or a confession like a grenade just when life feels calm. Trust here isn't built slowly; it gets broken, rebuilt, and upgraded in jolts. You're both a little addicted to the shock of the reveal. The trap: using surprise disclosures to test whether the other will stay. The move: tell the hard truth on a quiet Tuesday, not in the middle of a crisis you created.",
    Sagittarius: "You two are happiest when you've booked a one-way ticket or joined some philosophy nobody back home understands. Your beliefs keep evolving, and every year one of you arrives with a new worldview, a new diet, or a new plan to live abroad. Friends can't keep track, and your families assume it's a phase. Restlessness is the glue, and it's also the crack, because the one who wants to stay put gets labeled boring. The trap: treating each new adventure as proof that you're still free. The move: plan the trips together, and let one of you veto a destination without being called small.",
    Capricorn: "You two refuse the corporate ladder and the white-picket timeline, and it shows in your job choices, your odd career pivots, and the way you both laugh at five-year plans. One of you walks away from a stable position at least once, and the other has to decide whether to panic or cheer. You build ambition in unusual shapes, side businesses, remote gigs, projects your parents don't get. The trap: sabotaging success the moment it starts to look conventional. The move: pick one long goal you both commit to for real, and rebel everywhere else.",
    Aquarius: "You two are friends first, lovers second, and you'd both be offended if anyone flipped that order. Your social circle is wide and strange, and one of you always has a new person the other is expected to adore instantly. Private time gets swallowed by group chats, causes, and late nights with the crew. When closeness gets heavy, you both retreat into ideas. The trap: acting so evolved about jealousy that neither of you admits the new friend is a problem. The move: say the petty feeling out loud, laugh at it, and then protect two nights a week for just the two of you.",
    Pisces: "You two drift in and out of each other's reality, and some weeks it feels like you share one dream, other weeks like roommates on opposite sides of town. You both disappear, into music, spirituality, sleep, a screen, and return without explaining where you went. Intuition runs the relationship more than logic, and sudden gut decisions reshape your life overnight. The partner who needs a plan feels abandoned in the fog. The trap: vanishing emotionally and calling it 'needing space.' The move: before you check out, give a simple signal, a word, a text, so the other knows you're coming back.",
  },
  Neptune: {
    Aries: "You two fell for the fantasy of being each other's rescuer or warrior, and part of you still expects the other to charge in and fix everything. When one of you acts selfishly, the other excuses it as passion. Anger gets blurry here: you rarely fight cleanly, and resentment leaks out as sulking, sarcasm, or a slammed door with no explanation. You idealize the other's courage and then feel betrayed when they're scared. The trap: pretending you're not angry until it explodes sideways. The move: say 'I'm mad about this specific thing' in one sentence, and let the other be human instead of heroic.",
    Taurus: "You two dream about a beautiful life, the house, the garden, the good wine, and quietly avoid looking at what it costs. Money gets fuzzy between you: who paid, what's shared, what was a gift. You soothe each other with food, touch, and shopping, and it works so well that nobody notices the debt or the extra weight creeping in. The romance lives in the senses, and so does the escape. The trap: buying the feeling instead of building it. The move: open the bank app together once a week, no blame, and name one pleasure that costs nothing.",
    Gemini: "You two say beautiful things to each other and then remember the conversation completely differently. Texts get misread, promises get made casually and forgotten, and both of you swear you said it clearly. You share a private language of references and half-sentences that feels like telepathy, until it isn't. One of you tells small smoothing lies to keep the peace, and the other senses it without proof. The trap: trusting the vibe of a conversation instead of its content. The move: for anything that matters, dates, money, plans, repeat it back and put it in writing.",
    Cancer: "You two fantasize about the perfect family home and feel crushed when real holidays involve sulking relatives and burnt food. You mother each other to the point of losing track of whose feelings are whose; when one of you is sad, the other absorbs it whole. Old family patterns sneak into your kitchen dressed up as love. The couch becomes a hiding place from the world. The trap: rescuing each other's moods instead of letting each person feel their own. The move: when one of you is low, ask 'do you want help or company?' and believe the answer.",
    Leo: "You two are in love with the story of your love, the meet-cute you retell, the grand gestures, the idea that you're special. It's genuinely romantic, and it also makes ordinary Tuesdays feel like failure. You both perform the relationship a little for friends and online, and privately wonder if the real thing matches the picture. Kids, creative projects, or a shared dream get loaded with fantasy. The trap: chasing the high of the early chapters and resenting the present one. The move: celebrate one boring win together each week, out loud, like it's the big scene.",
    Virgo: "You two blur the line between caring for each other and caretaking each other. One of you ends up nursing, managing, or quietly fixing the other's life, and calls it love while running on fumes. Health worries get vague and anxious, and the chores pile up in a haze of good intentions. You both believe you're the one doing more, and neither has counted. The trap: silent martyrdom followed by a meltdown about the laundry. The move: list who does what for one week, honestly, and say the unglamorous need before it turns into resentment.",
    Libra: "You two fell for the ideal of the perfect partnership and still measure yourselves against it. Conflict gets smoothed over so fast that nobody knows what you actually disagree about. You mirror each other's tastes and opinions until one of you wakes up unsure what they even like. Outsiders call you the dream couple, and that pressure keeps the cracks hidden. The trap: keeping the peace by disappearing into the other person. The move: each of you names one thing you want that the other doesn't, and you let that difference stand without fixing it.",
    Scorpio: "You two feel soul-bonded, and that intensity makes it hard to see clearly. Suspicion floats in the air without evidence: a phone face down, a late reply, a name that came up twice. Sex is where you merge completely and also where you escape real conversations. Secrets are romanticized between you, and something always stays in the shadows. The trap: reading each other's minds and acting on the paranoid version. The move: ask the direct question you're scared of, 'are you hiding something?', and accept a plain answer instead of hunting for the hidden one.",
    Sagittarius: "You two share a big vision, a spiritual path, a move abroad, a dream life that's always one trip away. Believing in each other is your gift; believing in the plan while ignoring the budget is your habit. Faith covers a lot of problems, and you both talk about growth more than you schedule it. One of you gets swept up in a guru, a teacher, or a philosophy, and the other follows half-convinced. The trap: waiting for the big someday instead of living the ordinary now. The move: pick one dream and put a date and a dollar amount on it this month.",
    Capricorn: "You two idealize the life you're supposed to build, the status, the stability, the picture of having made it, and you're not sure whose picture it is. Career sacrifices get made in the name of the future and never quite discussed. One of you props up the other's ambitions and slowly disappears into the role. Duty feels holy here, and exhaustion gets called commitment. The trap: working toward a goal neither of you actually chose. The move: sit down and ask each other, plainly, 'if nobody were watching, what would we want?' and act on one answer.",
    Aquarius: "You two believe in the friendship at the heart of this, and in a group of friends who feel like chosen family, and you both get hurt when those people turn out to be ordinary. Ideals about freedom and honesty sound great, yet the lines around exes, flirty friends, and group chats stay suspiciously vague. You're both better at loving humanity than at saying what you need tonight. The trap: agreeing to an open-minded arrangement one of you secretly hates. The move: talk about the specific people, by name, and say where the line is before someone crosses it.",
    Pisces: "You two feel like you've known each other forever, and some nights the connection is so complete it's almost spiritual. That's also why you both ignore the obvious: the drinking, the scrolling, the bills, the thing nobody wants to name. The edges dissolve until you can't tell your mood from the other's. You forgive endlessly and rarely hold anyone to anything. The trap: calling escape a shared sanctuary and letting real life slide. The move: choose one reality check each week, a budget, a hard talk, a sober evening, and treat it as an act of love.",
  },
  Pluto: {
    Aries: "You two turn small decisions into wars of will, and the fight is rarely about the restaurant. Whoever backs down first feels like they lost something bigger. The chemistry is ferocious, and so is the temper, and both of you secretly respect the other more after a blowout. Control shows up as speed: one of you acts first so the other can't object. The trap: making every disagreement a test of who is stronger. The move: when the heat spikes, one of you calls a twenty-minute break, and you come back to argue about the actual issue, not who wins.",
    Taurus: "You two fight about money and possessions with an intensity that surprises you both. Whose name is on the lease, who paid for the car, who owns the furniture after all: these carry the real power. One of you controls by holding the purse, the other by withholding affection or comfort. Change comes slowly and then violently, a years-long standoff broken by one massive move. The trap: using security as leverage. The move: make the finances fully transparent, every account visible to both, and watch how much of the tension drains out.",
    Gemini: "You two control each other with words: the perfect cutting remark, the reread message, the screenshot saved for later. Arguments turn into cross-examinations, and both of you remember exact phrasing from months ago. One of you checks the other's phone or social activity, and the other knows it. Conversations can transform you, but they can also become interrogations. The trap: using information as a weapon instead of a bridge. The move: agree that nothing from a past fight gets quoted in a new one, and delete the screenshots you're keeping as ammunition.",
    Cancer: "You two hold power through the home and the family, who cooks, who hosts, whose mother gets the holidays. Emotional pressure is the weapon of choice: guilt, tears, the cold kitchen when someone is in trouble. Old wounds from both your childhoods get replayed under your roof, and you both know exactly where to press. When it heals, it heals down to the roots. The trap: controlling each other through caretaking and sulking. The move: name the family pattern when you spot it, 'this is my dad's move,' and choose not to finish it.",
    Leo: "You two compete for the spotlight, and jealousy flares when the other gets more attention at the party or more praise at work. Pride is the power currency: whoever feels less admired pulls away or punishes with coldness. The romance is dramatic, all-or-nothing, and neither of you tolerates being taken for granted. You both want to be the one who matters most. The trap: making love a contest for who gets adored harder. The move: praise each other in public before anyone else can, and say 'I felt invisible tonight' instead of starting the silent war.",
    Virgo: "You two wrestle for control in the small stuff: how the dishwasher is loaded, how the money is budgeted, whose health routine is correct. Criticism becomes a quiet form of dominance, and one of you ends up feeling permanently not good enough. You're both obsessive about doing things right, and that obsession can rebuild your whole lives for the better. The trap: fixing each other until one of you breaks. The move: before correcting anything, ask whether it actually matters; if it doesn't, let the towel stay folded wrong.",
    Libra: "You two keep a hidden scorecard of fairness, and power moves happen politely. Nobody yells; instead, someone agrees sweetly and then does whatever they wanted anyway. Jealousy about outsiders runs deep, charming friends, coworkers, the ex who's still around. The relationship itself is the battleground, and both of you fear losing the upper hand in it. The trap: manipulating through niceness so no one can call it a fight. The move: say what you want directly, even if it sounds selfish, and let the other say no without paying for it later.",
    Scorpio: "You two go all the way in, and there's no halfway version of this relationship. Jealousy, possessiveness, and sexual intensity are baked in, and each of you knows the other's darkest corners. Betrayal, real or feared, is the nightmare you circle around. Every crisis either destroys something or burns it into something stronger. The trap: testing loyalty with provocations, the flirting, the silence, the threat to leave. The move: make one pact about the dealbreakers, spoken out loud, and stop checking whether the other will keep it.",
    Sagittarius: "You two fight over whose beliefs run the house: religion, politics, how to raise kids, which truth is the truth. One of you tends to preach and the other resists being converted. Travel or study transforms you both, and the trip abroad or the course that changed everything is a turning point in your story. Freedom becomes a control issue when one of you wants to roam and the other holds the reins. The trap: winning the debate and losing the partner. The move: admit one thing the other has taught you that changed your mind.",
    Capricorn: "You two are a power couple in the making, and ambition sits at the center of your bond. Control shows up through career decisions, who moves for whose job, whose success gets priority. One of you plays authority figure, the other chafes and then quietly takes over. You build impressive things together and neglect tenderness along the way. The trap: turning the relationship into a business where love is earned by performance. The move: schedule one evening a week with no plans, no goals, no talk of work, and guard it like a deadline.",
    Aquarius: "You two exercise power through detachment: whoever cares less holds the control. Friendships and group loyalties become flashpoints, and one of you feels outranked by the circle, the cause, or the online community. You both want to change the world and sometimes treat each other like a project to upgrade. Sudden cold withdrawals do more damage than yelling. The trap: pretending not to need each other to stay in charge. The move: say 'I need you' plainly, once a week, and notice how much power it gives back instead of taking.",
    Pisces: "You two hold power through sacrifice and victimhood, and it's hard to see because it looks like devotion. Whoever suffers more gets the moral high ground, and the other feels endlessly guilty. Addictions, escapes, or secrets have a way of surfacing between you and forcing total change. Spiritual or creative life is where you transform each other deeply. The trap: rescuing and being rescued as a way of keeping the other hooked. The move: each of you owns one problem as fully yours, and the other stops trying to save it.",
  },
  "North Node": {
    Aries: "You two keep defaulting to keeping the peace, deferring, asking 'what do you want?' until nobody wants anything. The relationship is pushing you both to take a position, even a clumsy one. Every time one of you says 'I want this' without a disclaimer, something opens up between you. It feels rude at first, almost dangerous. The trap: slipping back into polite accommodation and resenting it privately. The move: once a week, each of you makes a decision for the couple, the dinner, the movie, the plan, and the other goes along without editing it.",
    Taurus: "You two are hooked on drama, crisis, and intensity, and calm feels suspicious. This relationship is asking you to slow down and build something steady: a routine, a savings account, a weekend that's boring on purpose. Every time you pick the stable option, it feels like losing the spark, and every time it gets easier. The trap: stirring up a fight because peace feels like boredom. The move: create one simple ritual, a shared breakfast, a weekly walk, and keep it going for three months no matter what emotional storm is brewing.",
    Gemini: "You two love the big picture, the grand theories and the someday plans, and skip the small conversations that actually hold a life together. This relationship is pushing you to ask questions instead of delivering sermons, and to listen to the details of each other's day. Curiosity is the growth edge; certainty is the rut. The trap: lecturing each other about who's right about life. The move: every night, each of you asks one genuine question you don't know the answer to, and the other answers without turning it into a philosophy.",
    Cancer: "You two are wired for achievement and public image, and the relationship keeps dragging you home. It's asking you to prioritize feelings, family, and the private life over the career and the reputation. Saying 'I'm scared' or 'I need you' feels weaker than finishing the project, and that is exactly the lesson. The trap: hiding in work and calling it building a future together. The move: protect one evening a week at home with no screens and no work talk, and let one of you be taken care of without earning it.",
    Leo: "You two hide in the group, the friends, the cause, the crowd, and hold back from being fully seen as a couple. This relationship is pushing you both to take personal risks: to play, to create, to show off a little, to admit you want to be adored. It feels exposing and a bit selfish. The trap: staying cool and detached so nobody can reject you. The move: do one thing together that puts you on display, a party you host, a project you share, a public declaration, and let yourselves enjoy the attention.",
    Virgo: "You two slip easily into dreaming, drifting, and letting things slide until they become a mess. This relationship is pushing you toward real-world care: showing up on time, keeping the promises, cleaning the kitchen, going to the doctor. The growth is in the unglamorous details, and it feels fated because life keeps forcing the issue. The trap: waiting for inspiration or rescue instead of doing the task. The move: pick three small daily habits you both commit to, write them on the fridge, and treat completing them as how you say 'I love you.'",
    Libra: "You two are both used to running your own lives and doing it alone, and this relationship is the course in real partnership. Compromise feels like defeat at first, and asking for help feels like weakness. Every time one of you considers the other's view before acting, the bond deepens in a way that surprises you both. The trap: retreating into independence the moment it gets hard. The move: before any decision that affects both of you, ask 'what do you think?' and wait for the full answer before you move.",
    Scorpio: "You two are comfortable with comfort: the easy routine, the stable finances, the pleasant surface. This relationship is pushing you into the deep end, the real conversations about sex, money, death, jealousy, the things you both avoid. It feels unsettling, even threatening, and it's exactly where you grow closest. The trap: choosing a nice evening over an honest one, again and again. The move: once a month, each of you tells the other one truth you've been holding back, and neither of you is allowed to punish the other for it.",
    Sagittarius: "You two can talk a topic to death, gather opinions, compare options, and never actually leap. This relationship is pushing you toward faith, adventure, and a shared sense of meaning bigger than the daily chatter. The move abroad, the pilgrimage, the belief you commit to together keeps knocking. The trap: researching the dream until it expires. The move: pick one big adventure, book it within thirty days, and stop asking everyone else what they think of it.",
    Capricorn: "You two are pulled back toward the nest, toward feelings and family comfort, and this relationship is asking you to build something in the world. Commitment here means structure: a plan, a shared goal, a public role you take on as a couple. It feels cold at first compared to cozy, and it's where your respect for each other grows. The trap: hiding behind emotional needs to avoid responsibility. The move: set one concrete long-term goal with a deadline, write down who does what, and hold each other to it kindly.",
    Aquarius: "You two can make everything about your own little love story, and this relationship keeps pushing you outward. Friends, community, causes, and letting other people into your world are the growth edge. Being a couple that's part of something larger feels less romantic at first and ends up giving you both room to breathe. The trap: needing to be each other's everything and the center of every room. The move: join or build one group together, a club, a project, a circle of friends, and show up for it as a team.",
    Pisces: "You two try to control, organize, and fix your way through everything, and this relationship keeps asking you to surrender. Trust, compassion, and letting go of the checklist are the growth path. When life doesn't go to plan, the lesson is to hold each other rather than troubleshoot. It feels fated because every overmanaged situation keeps falling apart. The trap: criticizing each other for being imperfect. The move: once a week, do something together with no goal and no outcome, music, water, quiet, and forgive one thing without discussing it.",
  },
  "South Node": {
    Aries: "You two know how to sprint, and you slide back into it the second life gets hard: pick a fight, pick a project, pick a side, move. Whoever reacts first wins, so neither of you waits long enough to hear the other finish a sentence. It feels alive, and it feels exactly like every blowup you have already had, word for word. Friends have watched you break up and make up in the same weekend. The trap: treating speed as honesty and slamming doors to prove you care. The move: when the heat rises, one of you says 'give me ten minutes,' and the other lets it happen without chasing.",
    Taurus: "The old groove between you is the couch, the same takeout order, the same show, and a quiet agreement not to rock anything. It is genuinely soothing, which is why you two keep choosing it over the trip, the move, the harder conversation. Months vanish and you both wonder why the relationship feels heavy when nothing is wrong. One of you hoards comfort, the other hoards money, and both call it being sensible. The trap: mistaking stuck for safe. The move: book one thing this month that costs a little more than feels reasonable and scares you both slightly, then actually go.",
    Gemini: "You two fall back into talking about everything except the thing. Hours of banter, voice notes, theories about your friends' relationships, and the real question sits untouched under the jokes. It feels like closeness because the words never stop, and it is familiar because you have been doing this since the first week. When one of you gets serious, the other changes the subject with something funny and you both laugh with relief. The trap: being endlessly entertaining so nobody has to be vulnerable. The move: once a week, put the phones in another room and each finish the sentence 'what I have not told you is.'",
    Cancer: "When the world gets loud, you two retreat into the nest and pull the blanket over your heads. You feed each other, fuss over each other, cancel plans, and call it self-care. It works for a night and then it becomes a month of hiding. One of you slips into parenting the other, and the other slips into letting it happen, and resentment starts to smell like home cooking. Friends stop inviting you because you always say no. The trap: making the relationship a bunker. The move: say yes to the next invitation you both want to decline, and stay past the first hour.",
    Leo: "The familiar script between you is a show: grand gestures, public declarations, big reconciliations with an audience. You two know how to make each other feel like stars, and you slide back into needing that spotlight to feel loved. When the applause stops, one of you starts a small drama just to get the other's full attention back. Your friends can recite your greatest fights because you performed them in front of everyone. The trap: confusing being admired with being known. The move: do one loving thing a week that nobody sees, never gets mentioned, and never gets posted.",
    Virgo: "The rut you two fall into is fixing each other. You trade notes on posture, spending, the way the dishwasher got loaded, and it feels like care because it used to be care. Every weekend turns into a to-do list and romance gets scheduled after the errands, which means never. One of you criticizes, the other over-apologizes, and you have both played these roles so long you could swap scripts. The trap: treating the relationship as a project that is never finished. The move: go one full day without correcting anything, and notice how badly each of you wants to.",
    Libra: "You two slide back into keeping the peace at any cost. Where to eat, whose parents for the holidays, whether that comment hurt: every answer becomes 'whatever you want,' and nobody ever gets what they want. It feels gracious and grown-up, and it has the flavor of a relationship you have both lived before. The anger does not disappear, it leaks out as sighs and sudden coldness about something unrelated. Outsiders call you the perfect couple, and you both quietly hate that. The trap: politeness as a hiding place. The move: each of you states one real preference a day and lets the other disagree.",
    Scorpio: "The groove between you is crisis. When things get calm, one of you goes looking through the phone, the past, the tone of a text, and finds something to be intense about. It feels like the deepest part of the relationship because that is where you first felt fused. Makeup nights after the storm are unforgettable, so neither of you wants to give the storm up. Your closest friends have learned not to ask how it is going. The trap: needing a threat to feel the bond. The move: let a quiet week stay quiet, and tell each other out loud that boring is allowed.",
    Sagittarius: "When things get real, you two leave. A spontaneous trip, a new philosophy, a plan to move abroad: anything bigger and brighter than the bill that is overdue or the conversation you owe each other. It feels like freedom and it feels exactly like the last time you ran. You both preach honesty and then deliver it like a lecture, then book flights before the other replies. Friends love your stories and notice you are never home. The trap: using the horizon to avoid the kitchen table. The move: before the next escape, sit down and handle one boring, specific problem together, start to finish.",
    Capricorn: "You two default to duty. Work first, obligations second, each other when the calendar allows, and somehow that time never arrives. The relationship runs like a small company, efficient and joyless, and you both recognize it because you have done this before. One of you becomes the responsible adult and the other either rebels or shrinks. Affection turns into logistics texts: pick up the dry cleaning, did you pay it. The trap: earning love by being useful instead of simply having it. The move: put one unproductive, pointless date on the calendar every week and guard it like a meeting with the boss.",
    Aquarius: "The old pattern between you two is cool distance dressed up as maturity. You give each other so much space you end up roommates with great opinions. Feelings get turned into theories, and every argument becomes a debate about principles rather than 'I missed you.' You fall back into group hangs because a crowd is easier than two people alone. Friends think you are the most relaxed couple they know, and neither of you corrects them. The trap: detachment that looks like trust. The move: say the needy thing out loud, the one that feels embarrassing, and let the other respond without analyzing it.",
    Pisces: "You two drift. When life presses in, you slide into sleeping late, a second bottle, endless scrolling side by side, or rescuing whichever of you is sinking harder. It feels tender and fated and it is also how months dissolve without a single decision. One of you plays the savior, the other plays the one who needs saving, and the roles quietly swap. Boundaries go blurry, and resentment shows up as vague sadness nobody can name. The trap: calling escape intimacy. The move: pick one concrete thing a week that you both do sober, awake, and on time, and follow through.",
  },
  Chiron: {
    Aries: "The sore spot between you two is wanting to come first and feeling selfish for it. One of you learned early that anger got you punished, so when the other raises their voice, the room goes cold and someone freezes. You both flinch from asking directly, then resent not getting. Small moments reopen it: being ignored at a party, the other making a plan without asking. The trap: swallowing the want until it explodes over something tiny. The healing: practice clean asks, 'I want this, now,' and let the other say yes without either of you apologizing for the request.",
    Taurus: "Between you two lives an old fear of not having enough, money, affection, time, and of not being worth it. One of you checks the bank balance compulsively, the other overbuys to feel safe, and both flinch when a gift feels too expensive. A casual comment about spending lands like a verdict on who you are. The wound reopens around rent, raises, and whose name is on things. The trap: measuring love in security and coming up short every time. The healing: say out loud what each of you is worth to the other, specifically, before you ever talk about the budget.",
    Gemini: "The wound you share is feeling unheard or stupid. One of you was talked over growing up, the other was the kid who got corrected, and now a simple misunderstanding feels like proof you do not get each other. Texts get reread five times for tone. Being interrupted stings far more than it should, and you both know it. The trap: rehearsing arguments in your heads and then saying the sharp version. The healing: when a conversation turns, one of you repeats back what the other said before responding, and you keep doing it until the other says 'yes, that.'",
    Cancer: "What hurts between you two is belonging. One or both of you came from a home that was not safe to be soft in, and together you rebuild that ache and that hope. Holidays with family reopen it every year. A partner working late, forgetting a birthday dinner, or siding with their mother lands as abandonment. You mother each other fiercely and then feel smothered. The trap: making each other pay for old kitchens. The healing: create your own rituals that belong to nobody's family, and say 'you are home to me' on the bad nights, not just the good ones.",
    Leo: "The wound between you is not being seen, and the shame of wanting to be. One of you grew up as background, the other as the one who had to perform for love, and together you notice every unreturned compliment. A partner scrolling during your story feels devastating. You both downplay wins and then sulk when they go uncelebrated. The trap: waiting to be noticed instead of asking to be. The healing: make pride a habit, name one thing you admire in each other every week, and throw a real celebration for the next win, however small it looks.",
    Virgo: "What you two share is the voice that says you are never good enough. Bodies, jobs, cooking, the way you load the car: you both notice the flaw first. Criticism from each other cuts to the bone because it matches the voice already there. One of you overworks to earn rest, the other gets sick when the stress hits. The trap: turning the relationship into another place to be graded. The healing: when one of you slips into self-attack, the other names it gently, 'that is the old voice,' and you both stop fixing and simply sit down together.",
    Libra: "The ache you two carry is about partnership itself: old breakups, parents who split, being left right when you finally relaxed. So you work very hard at fairness, and a lopsided moment, one of you giving more this month, feels like the beginning of the end. You avoid conflict because conflict once meant someone left. The trap: keeping score to prevent abandonment, which slowly creates it. The healing: have the uncomfortable disagreement and stay in the room afterward, then say 'I am still here' until both of you believe that a fight is not an exit.",
    Scorpio: "The wound between you is trust. At least one of you has been lied to or cheated on, and the relationship keeps brushing against that scar. A locked phone, a friend you have not met, a delayed reply sends one of you spiraling while the other feels accused. Sex is both the place you feel safest and the place you feel most exposed. The trap: testing each other to see if the betrayal is coming. The healing: offer transparency before it is demanded, and when the fear hits, say 'I am scared' instead of asking a trap question.",
    Sagittarius: "What hurts between you two is meaning and faith. One or both of you were sold a belief that broke, religion, a family story, a dream that collapsed, and now you are suspicious of anything that sounds too hopeful. Plans for the future make you both a little nauseous. When one of you gets excited, the other pokes holes to protect them. The trap: cynicism as armor, so nothing big ever gets tried. The healing: pick one shared belief you actually hold, write it down, and take one real risk on it together this year.",
    Capricorn: "The shared wound is failure and disappointing someone with authority. Somebody's father, boss, or a career that stalled left a mark, and you two feel it every time money gets tight or a promotion goes to someone else. Each of you secretly worries the other will see you as a letdown. So you both overwork, go silent about struggle, and act more fine than you are. The trap: hiding setbacks until they become disasters. The healing: tell each other about the small failure the same day it happens, and answer it with respect instead of advice.",
    Aquarius: "The wound between you two is being the odd one out. Both of you have been the weird kid, the one who did not fit in the group, and you found each other partly because of it. But group settings still reopen it: a party where one of you clicks and the other feels left behind, a friend circle that picks a side. You both pull away before you can be excluded. The trap: detaching first so rejection cannot land. The healing: agree on a signal at gatherings that means 'come find me,' and actually go when you see it.",
    Pisces: "What you two share is grief that never got a name: a parent who drank, a loss nobody talked about, a childhood spent caretaking someone else. You recognize it in each other instantly, which is why this feels so tender and so heavy. One of you disappears when things hurt, the other tries to rescue, and both end up drained. The trap: bonding over pain until pain is the glue. The healing: get help from outside the two of you, a therapist, a group, a ritual, and let the relationship be the place you rest, not the only place you heal.",
  },
  MC: {
    Aries: "People know you two as the couple that just does it. You announce the move, the business, the marathon, and you are already halfway there before anyone reacts. Together you are braver in public than either of you is alone, and that reputation opens doors. Friends call you when they need someone to say 'quit, go.' The downside: you launch faster than you finish, and people have noticed the unfinished ventures. The trap: needing to be first so badly you skip the plan. The move: before the next big announcement, finish one thing and let people see you complete it.",
    Taurus: "Out in the world, you two are the couple with their life together: the good address, the reliable jobs, the dinner party where the food is excellent. People trust you with money and ask your advice on buying things. Building something tangible together, property, a business, a savings goal, is where you shine. The shadow is that outsiders think you are rigid, and you both secretly wonder if you have played it too safe. The trap: letting comfort become your whole public identity. The move: make one visible, surprising career choice together that your friends would never predict.",
    Gemini: "You two are known as the couple who know everyone. You are the connectors, the ones with the group chat, the side project, the podcast idea, the newsletter. Your joint reputation is being interesting, and you work best together in anything involving talking, writing, or selling. The downside: people are never quite sure what you actually do. The trap: spreading across six ideas so none become a real career win. The move: pick the one shared project people keep asking about, give it a deadline, and tell everyone you know so you cannot back out.",
    Cancer: "People see your home as the hub. Holidays happen at your place, friends crash on your couch, and anyone going through a rough patch knows your door is open. Together you are drawn to work that takes care of people, and a family business or a shared caring profession fits you. The public story is that you two are family to everyone. The trap: giving so much to the extended circle that your own ambitions stay in the drawer. The move: protect one career goal as fiercely as you protect your people, and say it out loud at the next dinner.",
    Leo: "You two are the couple people talk about. The entrance, the photos, the wedding everyone still mentions, the creative venture with your faces on it. Together you are meant to be visible, and you do your best work when someone is watching. People either adore you as a pair or roll their eyes, and you feel both. The trap: building a public image that has to be maintained even when things at home are rough. The move: put your joint spotlight behind something you are proud of beyond yourselves, a show, a cause, a brand, and let that take the stage.",
    Virgo: "Your reputation is competence. You two are the people friends call to fix the resume, plan the move, sort the taxes, organize the wedding. At work together you are precise, dependable, and quietly excellent. The problem is that people see you as helpers, not leaders, and you both sometimes resent being the reliable ones. The trap: doing flawless work for other people's dreams while yours wait. The move: charge properly for what you already do for free, and put your joint skill behind a project that has your names on it.",
    Libra: "Out in the world, you two are the gracious couple: great hosts, good at introductions, the pair who calm a room. People bring you into their conflicts to mediate. Together you shine in work involving design, law, negotiation, events, or anything where taste and diplomacy matter. The shadow is that your public face is so pleasant nobody sees the tension underneath. The trap: saying yes to every invitation and collaboration to keep your image intact. The move: turn down one prestigious offer that does not fit, and let people see that you two have standards.",
    Scorpio: "People are fascinated by you two and cannot quite read you. You keep your business private, your fights unposted, and your ambitions quiet until they land. Together you are strong in work involving money, research, crisis, or anything others find too intense. Rumors follow you because silence invites them. The trap: guarding privacy so hard that you miss support and opportunities you would have gotten by talking. The move: pick one trusted person in your field and let them in on a real plan, and watch how quickly doors open.",
    Sagittarius: "You two are known as the adventurers. The couple who moved countries, who teach, who went back to school at the same time, who always have a story from somewhere. Together your work leans toward travel, education, publishing, or anything with a big idea behind it. People find you inspiring and slightly unreliable. The trap: chasing the next horizon so often that nothing compounds. The move: turn your experiences into one teachable, lasting thing, a course, a book, a business, and stay put long enough to build it.",
    Capricorn: "People see you two as the serious couple, the ones building an empire. Careers are central, titles matter, and together you climb faster than either could alone. Colleagues respect you, and family relies on you. The downside is that outsiders assume the relationship is a merger, and on bad weeks so do you. The trap: letting the ladder decide every choice, from where you live to when you have kids. The move: write down the success you two want in plain words, then cut one obligation that does not serve it.",
    Aquarius: "You two are the unconventional couple. Separate bedrooms, a startup, an open-door friend group, a cause you organize around. People come to you for the future, the new idea, the community project. Your public identity is being different, and it attracts both fans and critics. The trap: rebelling against every expectation so reflexively that you reject opportunities just because they look normal. The move: choose one mainstream platform or role and use it for your odd, brilliant idea instead of staying on the fringe.",
    Pisces: "Your public image is soft-focus. People see you two as artistic, spiritual, healing, a little mysterious, and nobody can quite explain what you do for a living. Together you are drawn to creative work, caregiving, music, film, or anything that moves people. The shadow is confusion: undercharging, vague plans, being used by people who admire you. The trap: waiting to be discovered. The move: give your shared work a name, a price, and a place people can find it, and treat the practical side as part of the art.",
  },
  Vesta: {
    Aries: "You two throw yourselves at a challenge together: training for something, starting a business, fighting for a cause. When there is a goal, you are unstoppable as a team. The problem is that intimacy starts to feel like another workout. Sex gets efficient, conversations become strategy meetings, and neither of you notices the spark going flat until one of you snaps. The trap: turning every part of life into a competition you run side by side. The move: once a week, do something with no goal, no score, and no finish line, just the two of you messing around.",
    Taurus: "What you two devote yourselves to is building security: the home, the garden, the savings account, the perfect routine. You are both deeply loyal to that project, and it gives you a real sense of peace. But routine slowly eats desire. Friday nights become the same meal, the same show, the same pajamas, and one of you starts craving something neither can name. The trap: tending the life so carefully that you stop tending each other. The move: break one ritual on purpose each month, and spend the money you would have saved on pleasure.",
    Gemini: "You two are devoted to the conversation. Books, ideas, a shared project, a podcast, a running debate you have been having for years. The talking is sacred, and it is how you feel closest. But talk quietly replaces touch. You spend whole evenings in brilliant discussion and go to bed without a single kiss. The trap: living in your heads together while your bodies drift. The move: set a rule that the best conversations happen with physical contact, hands, feet, lying tangled together, and see what that does to the heat.",
    Cancer: "Your shared devotion is family: kids, pets, aging parents, the home everyone gathers in. You two are fierce protectors and the people you care for feel it. But somewhere along the way you became parents and caretakers first and lovers last. Date night gets canceled for someone else's emergency. The bedroom turns into a place to collapse. The trap: sacrificing the couple to keep the family running. The move: schedule time away from everyone who depends on you, a locked door, a night away, and treat it as essential to the family, not selfish.",
    Leo: "You two pour yourselves into something you create together: a band, a brand, a child, a home that looks like a magazine. Your devotion is to making something you are proud to show. When it shines, you both glow. When it demands everything, you stop performing for each other and save the charm for the audience. The trap: giving your best self to the project and your tired self to each other. The move: once a week, dress up, flirt, and put on the show for an audience of one, the person you are with.",
    Virgo: "You two are devoted to doing things right: the job, the health routine, the meal plan, the service you give others. There is real integrity in how you work together. The problem is that desire does not live on a schedule, and yours has quietly been filed under 'later.' Sex becomes one more task done well. One of you starts feeling like a coworker. The trap: optimizing a relationship that needs wasted time. The move: leave one evening a week deliberately unplanned and messy, and do not fix anything that goes wrong during it.",
    Libra: "The thing you two devote yourselves to is the relationship as a work of art: the aesthetic, the harmony, looking like the couple everyone admires. You put real care into keeping it beautiful. But beauty requires smoothing, and smoothing kills heat. You avoid the arguments that would clear the air and end up polite in bed. The trap: preserving the image of the relationship instead of the relationship. The move: have one honest, unflattering conversation a month, then let the passion from finally being real carry you somewhere.",
    Scorpio: "You two are devoted to each other with total focus: the bond, the secrets, the depth nobody else gets. It feels sacred. The danger is over-focus. When the relationship is the whole world, any small distance feels like betrayal, and passion curdles into monitoring. You both keep friends at arm's length to protect the intensity, then feel suffocated. The trap: obsession mistaken for devotion. The move: each of you keeps one friendship and one pursuit fully your own, and brings the stories home to share instead of guarding against them.",
    Sagittarius: "What you two devote yourselves to is a belief or a quest: a spiritual path, travel, study, a lifestyle bigger than ordinary life. You feel most alive side by side chasing meaning. But the mission starts to replace the romance. Every conversation becomes about the plan, the teaching, the next country, and the two of you as lovers get lost in the itinerary. The trap: being fellow pilgrims but not partners. The move: on the next trip or retreat, set aside a day with no agenda except each other, and stay in the room.",
    Capricorn: "You two are devoted to the long game: the career goals, the five-year plan, the reputation you are building. You are disciplined together, and it pays off. But desire does not survive being penciled in for after the quarterly targets. One of you starts working late and the other stops waiting up. The trap: believing you will get to romance once you are established, which never quite arrives. The move: treat pleasure as part of the plan now, with a fixed night each week that is non-negotiable and has nothing to do with work.",
    Aquarius: "You two devote yourselves to a cause or a community: activism, a collective, friends who feel like chosen family, a vision of the future. Together you are generous and principled. But you give so much of yourselves to the group that the private relationship runs on fumes. Intimacy gets intellectualized and your bedroom feels like a meeting room. The trap: loving humanity so well that you neglect the person next to you. The move: take a night off from the cause each week and give each other the attention you give the world.",
    Pisces: "Your shared devotion is spiritual or compassionate: meditation, recovery, art, helping people who are struggling. You two find something holy in serving together. The cost is that you dissolve into the mission. Your own needs look selfish to you, desire feels unspiritual, and the relationship becomes a sanctuary for everyone except you two. The trap: martyring the romance for a higher purpose. The move: treat pleasure as sacred too, and set a regular night that is only about your bodies, your joy, and nobody else's healing.",
  },
  Juno: {
    Aries: "You two committed before either of you had a plan, and you still treat loyalty like a race nobody wants to lose. Whoever says 'I love you' first, apologizes first, or books the trip first quietly wins a point, and the other keeps the tally. Jealousy flares hot and burns out in an hour, usually over who got more of the other's attention that week. You'd defend each other in a bar fight and then argue in the car about who started it. The trap: treating fairness as a scoreboard. The move: once a month, each of you names one thing the other did first, and let it count as a gift, not a point.",
    Taurus: "You two don't do fast promises; you do the lease, the shared account, the dog, and then one day you realize you're married in every way that matters. Loyalty between you looks like showing up with the same takeout order for the hundredth time. What sets off jealousy isn't flirting, it's anything that threatens the routine: a new friend who eats up Saturdays, a job offer in another city. You both dig in and call it stability when it's really fear of change. The trap: letting the relationship calcify into a comfortable habit neither of you chose on purpose. The move: renegotiate one household rule every season, out loud, like you're signing up again.",
    Gemini: "Your commitment lives in the conversation; the day you two stop talking about everything is the day you'd both feel single. You text through the workday, narrate each other's lives to friends, and a partner who goes quiet reads to the other as a breach of contract. Jealousy shows up as a raised eyebrow at the coworker who gets the good stories first. You both need variety, so the relationship keeps reinventing its roles, and nobody is sure who handles the bills this month. The trap: confusing constant chatter with actual agreements. The move: write down the three promises you're keeping this year and put them where you both see them.",
    Cancer: "You two commit like you're building a family, whether or not kids ever enter the picture, and within months you had a shared pantry, a standing holiday plan, and pet names nobody else is allowed to use. One of you slides into the caretaker role and the other lets it happen, then resents being mothered. In-laws are the real loyalty test: whose side you take at the dinner table gets remembered for years. The trap: keeping score of unpaid emotional labor while pretending you don't. The move: swap the caretaking roles for one full week and say, out loud, what it cost the other person all along.",
    Leo: "You two need to be chosen in public. A soft launch would have ended this relationship, and both of you know which photo made it official. Loyalty means taking each other's side loudly, in front of the group chat, the family, the ex. Jealousy isn't about sex, it's about spotlight: one of you shines at a party and the other goes cold on the drive home. You're proud of this bond and quietly terrified of looking foolish inside it. The trap: performing a happy couple while starving for private reassurance. The move: tell each other one specific thing you admire, with no audience, before bed at least twice a week.",
    Virgo: "You two show commitment through chores, and you both notice who did the dishes, who remembered the vet appointment, who refilled the soap. Fairness is a quiet obsession; neither of you would call it scorekeeping, but both of you could recite the ledger. Love lives in fixing each other's problems, which lands as criticism on bad days. Jealousy looks less like suspicion and more like 'why do you have time for them and not the laundry.' The trap: turning partnership into a performance review nobody asked for. The move: split the household list on paper, then retire the complaints about anything that was agreed to.",
    Libra: "You two built this on an unspoken contract: everything even, nobody the lesser partner. You split bills down to the cent, alternate whose family gets the holiday, and take turns choosing the restaurant. The problem is that keeping the peace becomes the job, and real resentment gets smoothed over with a polite 'it's fine.' Jealousy spikes when one of you is charming to someone else, because charm is your shared currency. The trap: staying balanced on the surface while one of you quietly carries more. The move: once a month, each of you names the thing that feels unfair, and nobody is allowed to say 'it's fine.'",
    Scorpio: "Loyalty between you two is all or nothing, and both of you would rather end it than be half-chosen. You know each other's passwords, or you've fought about why you don't. A friend's harmless comment about your partner gets filed and brought up months later. Betrayal is the fear underneath everything, so you test each other in small ways and call it curiosity. When it's good, nobody on earth is safer with you; when it's bad, it's an interrogation. The trap: surveillance dressed up as closeness. The move: agree on what counts as a breach of trust in plain words, and stop checking for anything outside that list.",
    Sagittarius: "You two committed on the condition that nobody gets caged, and you both flinch the second a promise starts sounding like a fence. Separate trips, separate friends, separate opinions about marriage, and somehow you keep coming back to each other. Jealousy isn't about other people; it's about one of you having an adventure the other wasn't invited to. You'd rather move across the world together than sign a joint lease. The trap: keeping one foot out the door so long it becomes a habit. The move: name one thing you're both fully in on for the next year, and plan the escape hatches around it, not through it.",
    Capricorn: "You two treat commitment like building a company, with roles, long-term plans, and a clear idea of what this looks like in ten years. Marriage, property, and reputation matter more than either of you admits, and you both know who handles money and who handles the family calendar. Loyalty means never embarrassing each other in front of people who matter. Jealousy shows up as resentment toward the other's career when it eats the weekend. The trap: running the relationship like an institution and forgetting to court each other. The move: book one evening a month with no logistics allowed, and whoever brings up a to-do pays for dinner.",
    Aquarius: "You two refuse the standard marriage script and have probably explained your arrangement to confused relatives more than once. Separate bedrooms, separate holidays, or a friendship that turned into a partnership with its own rules. Loyalty means respecting each other's independence, and the fastest way to wound either of you is to act possessive. Jealousy exists; you both just hide it behind being 'totally fine with it.' The trap: pretending you're too evolved to need reassurance. The move: admit one jealous feeling a month without apologizing for it, and let the other answer with something warmer than logic.",
    Pisces: "You two commit like it's a vow made somewhere before this life, and you both give until there's nothing left. One of you becomes the rescuer and the other the rescued, then the roles flip after a crisis, and nobody notices the pattern. The lines blur: your money, your friends, and your moods all merge. Jealousy stays unspoken and leaks out as sadness or distance. You forgive too much and resent it later in the dark. The trap: martyrdom posing as devotion. The move: each of you keeps one clear 'no' this month, says it kindly, and watches the relationship survive it.",
  },
  Lilith: {
    Aries: "Anger and desire sit very close together between you two, and neither of you fully trusts a relationship without a little fire. You pick fights that end in bed and would never admit that to your friends. Both of you hate being managed, soothed, or told to calm down, and the fastest way to lose the other is to handle them like a problem. There's a streak of 'us against the rules' that makes you reckless as a pair. The trap: using conflict as the only reliable route to heat. The move: say what you want directly, before the argument, and find out it works just as well without the shouting.",
    Taurus: "You two refuse to feel guilty about pleasure. Expensive dinners, long mornings in bed, the second bottle, the thing you bought and hid from the budget: this relationship indulges and dares anyone to judge it. Underneath is a stubborn possessiveness you both find more exciting than you'd say out loud. When someone tells you to be sensible, you double down together. The trap: indulgence becoming a way to avoid the harder conversations. The move: keep the pleasure, drop the secrecy, and put the splurges on the table so the thrill stays shared instead of turning into shame.",
    Gemini: "Your forbidden zone is what gets said. You two share the messages nobody else could read, the gossip you'd deny, the jokes that would end careers, and the texts that get deleted after. Secrets are erotic between you, and both of you love knowing something the room doesn't. The dark side is the double conversation: flirting elsewhere 'just for fun,' or telling a friend the version of the fight that flatters you. The trap: letting the thrill of secrecy leak into lying to each other. The move: keep the private language, but agree on one topic that never gets the edited version.",
    Cancer: "You two refuse to be domesticated on anyone else's terms, even while you build a home that swallows you both. Family disapproval hangs around this bond, whether it's the parent who never warmed up or the life you chose that nobody back home understands. Your hidden hunger is for total dependence, and it scares you both. You cling, then push away, then crawl back. The trap: letting old family wounds decide how much closeness is allowed. The move: say the ugly need out loud, 'I want you to need me,' and notice that nothing collapses when you do.",
    Leo: "You two are too much, and you've decided that's the point. You flirt in public, dress for each other, and enjoy the looks you get when you walk in together. Both of you secretly love being watched, and attention from outsiders is a charge you bring home. The shadow is ego: when one of you steals the room, the other feels erased and punishes it later. The trap: turning desire into a competition for who is more wanted. The move: stop hiding the hunger for admiration and feed it directly, in private, before either of you goes looking for it in a crowd.",
    Virgo: "Your rebellion is hidden inside rules. From the outside you two look tidy, responsible, almost boring, and privately you've built rituals, routines, and preferences nobody would guess. Control is part of the charge between you: who decides, who follows, who notices the smallest detail. The dark side is criticism used as a weapon, the cold correction that lands harder than a shout. The trap: shaming each other for the wants that don't fit your clean image. The move: write down one desire each that feels embarrassing, trade the papers, and respond only with curiosity.",
    Libra: "You two refuse to be the nice, balanced couple everyone assumes you are. Underneath the good manners is a taste for triangles: the ex who still texts, the friend who's a little too interested, the jealousy games you both pretend to be above. Charm is your shared weapon, and you both know exactly how to use it on outsiders to get a reaction at home. The trap: provoking jealousy to prove the other still cares. The move: stop outsourcing the tension, tell each other plainly what makes you feel wanted, and give it without needing a rival in the room.",
    Scorpio: "Obsession lives here, and you two know it. You've both gone through each other's history in detail, remembered names you shouldn't, and felt a thrill in how much power the other holds over you. Sex, secrets, and control are tangled together, and a fight can feel like the most honest moment you've had all week. Neither of you forgives easily or forgets at all. The trap: power struggles where losing feels like dying. The move: pick one arena where you deliberately hand control to the other, and let surrender be a choice instead of a defeat.",
    Sagittarius: "You two refuse to live by anyone's moral rulebook, and you've probably debated what monogamy even means more than once. Your taboo is freedom itself: the trip taken alone, the wild story you tell at dinner, the belief your families would never accept. Both of you get restless when the relationship starts feeling preachy. The dark side is carelessness, saying the brutal truth and calling it honesty. The trap: breaking rules just to prove nobody owns you, including each other. The move: set your own code together, in writing if needed, and keep it with the same pride you use to break everyone else's.",
    Capricorn: "Power is the hidden turn-on between you two. Ambition, status, who earns more, who has the upper hand in public: none of it is neutral, and both of you feel the charge. You play the respectable couple at work events while running private games about control. Resentment builds when one of you gets ahead, and it comes out cold and strategic, not loud. The trap: treating each other like competitors you're secretly trying to outrank. The move: name the power game out loud, decide on purpose when it's play and when it's off-limits, and never bring it into money decisions.",
    Aquarius: "You two refuse every label people try to stick on you. Your arrangement, your politics, your sex life, or your living situation looks odd from outside, and you both enjoy the confusion. The rebellion is real, but so is the coldness: when feelings get too big, one of you goes detached and calls it independence. You bond over being outsiders and quietly fear becoming ordinary. The trap: using freedom as a shield against needing each other. The move: once in a while, do the painfully normal couple thing, whether that's a dinner or a slow dance, and let yourselves admit you liked it.",
    Pisces: "Fantasy is where you two go wild. What happens between you lives half in imagination: the roles, the stories, the other lives you pretend to be living. Both of you are tempted to escape together, into late nights, substances, screens, or a private world that shuts everyone else out. The shadow is deception so gentle it doesn't feel like lying, like the thing unsaid or the version softened. The trap: disappearing into the dream until the real relationship starves. The move: keep the fantasy, but check in the next morning in plain daylight words about what was real and what you both want more of.",
  },
  Eros: {
    Aries: "The chase is the whole thing for you two. Desire spikes when one of you pursues and the other makes it hard, and it drops the second things get predictable. You're turned on by speed: the spontaneous kiss in the kitchen, the argument that flips into something else, the dare. Competition is foreplay, whether it's a game, a race, or who can make the other laugh first. The trap: waiting for a spark to happen instead of starting one. The move: take turns being the one who initiates, deliberately and without warning, and never let a full week pass without someone making the first move.",
    Taurus: "Slow is what gets you two going. Touch, scent, a long dinner, the good sheets, the hand resting on a thigh for an hour before anything happens. Rushing kills it; so does being on your phones. The body leads here, and both of you can tell instantly when the other is distracted. Food and physical comfort are part of the pull, which is why your best nights start in the kitchen. The trap: letting comfort turn into the same routine until nobody feels wanted anymore. The move: change one sensory detail each time, like a new place, a new texture, or a meal you've never cooked, and let it take all night.",
    Gemini: "Words are the turn-on between you two. Banter, teasing, the text that makes one of you blush in a meeting, the voice note you replay. The flirting never really stops, and a clever insult lands better than a compliment. When the conversation goes dull, so does the desire, fast. You both get bored of the same script and crave variety in how you connect. The trap: keeping all the heat in your phones and none in the room. The move: say one of those bold texts out loud, face to face, and watch what happens when the words have to survive eye contact.",
    Cancer: "Safety is what turns you two on. Desire rises when one of you feels truly held: the long hug after a bad day, the familiar smell of the pillow, being wanted at your least polished. Nostalgia is part of it; revisiting where you met or your old song still works. Rejection, even a small brush-off, shuts it all down for days. The trap: waiting to be pursued and feeling hurt when the other doesn't read your mood. The move: say 'come here' instead of hoping, and make the first touch of the evening something tender rather than something that asks for more.",
    Leo: "Being admired gets you two going. Dressing up for each other, the look across a crowded room, hearing out loud exactly what the other finds irresistible. Desire runs on being seen as the most wanted person alive, and neglect kills it faster than any fight. You both love a little theater: the night out, the reveal, the grand gesture. The trap: waiting to be adored first and sulking when the applause doesn't come. The move: praise one specific thing about the other's body or presence every single day, and plan one night a month that feels like an event.",
    Virgo: "Attention to detail is what turns you two on. Being studied, learning exactly what works, the partner who remembers the one small thing you mentioned once. Clean sheets, a calm room, and no mess on the counter matter more than either of you admits. Desire grows as you get skilled with each other, not from grand fantasy. The dark side is overthinking: one critical comment or a mental to-do list and the mood evaporates. The trap: treating intimacy like another task to do well. The move: ask each other one precise question about what you want, then give it without grading yourselves afterward.",
    Libra: "Courtship is the pull between you two. You want to be romanced, properly: the nice restaurant, the beautiful setting, the partner who still tries to look good for you after years. Harmony matters, so desire cools the moment there's unresolved tension in the air. You both love the mirroring, the matched rhythm, the feeling of being in step. The trap: avoiding conflict so hard that nothing sharp or surprising ever happens between you. The move: clear the air before date night, then book the kind of evening you'd plan for a first date and dress like you're still trying to win each other.",
    Scorpio: "Intensity is what hooks you two. Long eye contact, the secret nobody else knows, the feeling of being completely consumed. Casual doesn't register; either it's everything or it's nothing. Desire and power feel tangled, and a jealous flash does more than either of you would admit. You both crave being known down to the thing you're ashamed of. The trap: needing crisis or jealousy to feel the pull. The move: create the intensity on purpose, with phones off, a whole evening, and one honest confession each, so you never have to manufacture drama to get there.",
    Sagittarius: "Novelty turns you two on. Hotel rooms, a new city, the unplanned detour, laughing so hard in bed that you forget what you were doing. Desire lives in adventure, and nothing kills it faster than the same Tuesday night on repeat. You both love a partner who's up for anything and hate feeling watched or managed. The trap: blaming the relationship when it's really the routine that went flat. The move: put one new experience on the calendar every month, whether it's a trip, a class, or a place you've never kissed, and treat it as non-negotiable.",
    Capricorn: "Restraint is what gets you two going. Delayed gratification, the buttoned-up exterior, knowing what's coming later while you sit through the dinner party. Competence is attractive between you: watching the other handle something difficult sparks more than any compliment. Desire builds slowly and lasts. The downside is that exhaustion and work eat the evenings, and both of you treat intimacy like something you'll get to after the deadline. The trap: scheduling each other out entirely. The move: put it on the calendar without apology, and let the anticipation all day be part of the fun.",
    Aquarius: "Surprise and the mind turn you two on. The unexpected suggestion, the experiment, the conversation that goes somewhere strange at midnight and ends somewhere even stranger. Both of you get bored by anything that feels scripted or expected. Friendship is part of the chemistry, so a great debate works like foreplay. The weak spot is detachment: when one of you gets too in-the-head, the body gets forgotten. The trap: talking about trying new things instead of doing them. The move: each of you proposes one thing you've never done together, and you actually try both within the month.",
    Pisces: "Dissolving into each other is the pull for you two. Music, candlelight, water, the late night where you lose track of where one of you ends. Desire here is dreamy and wordless, and it vanishes the instant things feel transactional or rushed. You both respond to tenderness and imagination more than to technique. The trap: floating along waiting for a perfect mood that daily life never quite allows. The move: build the setting on purpose, with a playlist, a bath, and no phones, then tell each other one fantasy out loud so the dream has somewhere real to land.",
  },
  Psyche: {
    Aries: "You two find out who you really are to each other in the first ten seconds of a crisis, not in long talks. Trust gets built by showing up fast: the flat tire at midnight, the family blowup, the job loss. Neither of you can stand being handled carefully, so a soft, rehearsed confession reads as a lie. The hard part is slowing down long enough to let the other see the scared version under the bravado. The trap: turning every vulnerable moment into a dare and changing the subject once it lands. The move: when one of you admits something raw, the other stays seated and asks one more question.",
    Taurus: "Between you, trust is physical before it's verbal. You know you're safe when one of you falls asleep mid-sentence on the couch, or eats off the other's plate without asking. Deep intimacy arrives slowly and then refuses to leave, which is why a single broken promise about money or time sits in your bodies for months. You two show your whole selves through routine, not speeches. The trap: confusing comfort with closeness, so the real fears stay unspoken because dinner is nice and nobody wants to ruin it. The move: once a week, after the good meal, each of you names one thing you haven't said.",
    Gemini: "You two get to know each other's souls through talking, endlessly, in the car, over texts that run past 1 a.m., in voice notes nobody else would sit through. The test for you is whether the words are real. One of you is fluent at telling a charming version of the story, and the other can hear the edit. Being fully seen feels like being caught mid-joke with nowhere to hide. The trap: keeping intimacy clever and moving, so the heavy sentence never gets finished. The move: when the conversation gets close to something real, stop joking, put the phones face down, and finish that one sentence.",
    Cancer: "Between you, trust lives in the kitchen and the bed and the way one of you remembers exactly how the other takes their tea. You two let each other see the childhood stuff: the parent who left, the house that never felt safe. That is sacred, and it's also ammunition, and both of you know it. When hurt, you retreat into caretaking instead of confessing, so your partner makes you soup while you hide the actual wound. The trap: parenting each other instead of meeting as equals. The move: when one of you starts fussing, the other asks, 'What do you actually need from me right now?' and waits.",
    Leo: "You two need to feel adored by each other before you'll let the mask slip. Being fully seen is thrilling when it's the best version and terrifying when it's the jealous, needy one who wants to be chosen first at the party. Between you, loyalty gets proven in public: who defends whom in front of friends, who posts whom. Privately, each of you checks whether the love survives the unflattering moments. The trap: performing okay-ness for each other so nobody sees the insecure kid. The move: say the embarrassing need out loud, like 'I need you to tell me I matter tonight,' and the other says it back without teasing.",
    Virgo: "Trust between you gets built in the small print: the prescription picked up, the bill paid on time, the thing noticed and quietly fixed. You two see each other's flaws almost immediately, and that is either the most intimate thing about you or the most wounding. One of you hears every helpful suggestion as proof of not being good enough. Being fully known here means letting the other see the mess you haven't organized yet. The trap: improving each other as a substitute for accepting each other. The move: for one week, notice a flaw in your partner and say nothing except 'I love you like this.'",
    Libra: "You two are so good at being pleasant with each other that the real conversation keeps getting postponed. Intimacy feels like harmony, and the unspoken deal is that nobody ruins it. Underneath, each of you carries a quiet resentment that got smoothed over to keep dinner nice. Being fully seen means showing the part of you that disagrees, wants more, or isn't fine. The trap: agreeing your way into distance, until you're the lovely couple who secretly feel alone in the same room. The move: once a month, each of you says one thing you've been politely swallowing, and the other says 'thank you' before defending anything.",
    Scorpio: "Between you, trust is not given; it's earned through tests neither of you admits you're running. You two see through each other fast, which means lies don't last, but neither do the secrets you wanted to keep a little longer. Checking the phone, rereading the tone of a text three times, noticing who they looked at: it all happens, and it all gets filed. Once you do trust each other, it's total and almost frightening. The trap: using what you know about each other's deepest shame as leverage in a fight. The move: agree out loud that confessions are off-limits in arguments, forever, and hold to it.",
    Sagittarius: "You two open up while moving: on the road trip, on the hike, at the airport bar at 11 p.m. Sitting face to face to 'talk about us' makes one of you itch to leave. Your deepest bond is built on honesty so blunt it stings, and you'd both rather hear the brutal truth than feel managed. The shadow is that freedom becomes an escape hatch whenever intimacy gets heavy, and the other is left standing at the gate. The trap: turning deep feelings into a philosophy lecture so neither of you has to feel them. The move: next time it gets heavy, stay put for twenty minutes before anyone suggests going anywhere.",
    Capricorn: "You two trust slowly and on evidence. Neither of you believes words; you believe the person who shows up for the third year in a row. Vulnerability feels like weakness, so you handle each other's pain like a project: make a plan, fix the problem, move on. What goes unseen is the exhausted, frightened person under all the competence. Between you, the deepest intimacy happens when one of you finally admits 'I can't carry this.' The trap: being reliable partners who never actually cry in front of each other. The move: let the other watch you fail at something, and let them help without taking over.",
    Aquarius: "You two are best friends first, and that is exactly where your intimacy gets stuck. You can talk about anything except how much you need each other. Being fully seen feels like losing yourself, so one of you detaches right when things get close, cracking a joke or pivoting to some big idea. Your bond holds because you accept each other's weirdness without flinching. The trap: treating closeness like a theory you both agree on instead of something you let happen. The move: when one of you starts intellectualizing a feeling, the other says 'Okay, but how does it feel?' and neither answers with an opinion.",
    Pisces: "You two feel each other's moods from across the house, often before either of you knows what's wrong. The connection feels spiritual, almost telepathic, and that's beautiful until one of you expects the other to just know. Boundaries dissolve fast, and whose sadness is whose gets blurry. You forgive each other easily, too easily, and let real betrayals slip past because naming them would break the spell. The trap: loving the idealized soul instead of the actual person who forgot the plan again. The move: say what you need in plain words, even when it feels unromantic, and check the facts instead of the feeling.",
  },
  "Part of Fortune": {
    Aries: "Good things happen to you two when you move first. The apartment you grabbed the same day you saw it, the trip booked on a whim, the job one of you jumped at because the other said 'go.' You're happiest mid-adventure and grumpy when life turns administrative. Joy between you is loud: racing each other up the stairs, the competitive game night that gets out of hand. The trap: getting bored of your own good luck and starting a fight just to feel something. The move: when things feel flat, pick a physical challenge together, a race or a climb, instead of picking at each other.",
    Taurus: "Your luck as a couple arrives slowly and then compounds. The savings that quietly grew, the plant that finally bloomed, the favorite restaurant where they know your order. You two are happiest with good food, soft sheets, and a lazy weekend morning with nowhere to be, and outsiders are almost jealous of how content you look doing nothing. Money sticks with you once you stop chasing it. The trap: getting so attached to the comfortable setup that you refuse good changes, like the better city or the bigger job. The move: once a year, pick one comfort you'd trade for something new and actually trade it.",
    Gemini: "Things go right for you two through conversations and connections. The friend of a friend who had the apartment, the random chat at a bar that became a job lead. You're happiest talking nonsense on a long drive, swapping memes all day, planning five weekends you'll never take. Between you, laughter is the currency, and a day without a shared joke feels off. Your best breaks come from saying yes to the invite. The trap: scattering yourselves across so many plans and side projects that none of them pay off. The move: pick the one idea you both keep bringing up and give it a date on the calendar this month.",
    Cancer: "You two find your ease at home, and home keeps getting luckier. The rental that turned into a steal, the family recipe that became your tradition, the holiday everyone ends up wanting to spend at your place. Joy between you looks like cooking together badly, a movie under one blanket, the dog asleep between you. Family helps you out more than you expected, and you help them back. The trap: hiding in the nest so long that the outside world stops sending good things your way. The move: host once a month, open the door, and let the good luck walk in through other people.",
    Leo: "Good things find you two when you're seen. The toast that made the room cry, the photo that got shared everywhere, the party where people still talk about your entrance. You're happiest being a little extra together: dressing up for no reason, grand birthday plans, a creative project with both your names on it. Whatever you give away comes back to you in unexpected ways. The trap: needing an audience to feel happy, so quiet weeknights start to feel like failure. The move: create one private ritual that nobody else ever sees, and treat it like the best show you put on.",
    Virgo: "Your luck as a couple comes from getting the details right. The spreadsheet that caught the overcharge, the habit that fixed your sleep, the side hustle that works because one of you tracked every number. You two are happiest being useful together: reorganizing the garage, meal prepping for the week, helping a friend move. Satisfaction for you is a clean system that runs. The trap: turning every good day into a to-do list, so you forget to enjoy what you built. The move: every time you finish a project together, take one full evening off with zero improvements allowed.",
    Libra: "Things fall into place for you two through other people and through beauty. The introduction that changed your social life, the gorgeous flat you somehow afforded, the friends who set you up in the first place. You're happiest dressed well at a dinner for four, or picking out art for the wall and actually agreeing. As a pair you get treated well: doors open, people want you at the table. The trap: bending so much to keep everyone pleased that your own joy gets negotiated away. The move: plan one weekend that's entirely for the two of you, and turn down the invites without apologizing.",
    Scorpio: "Your luck arrives in the aftermath. You two find the good stuff after the crisis: the fresh start after the layoff, the payout nobody saw coming, the bond that got stronger once the worst secret came out. Joy between you is intense and private: late-night conversations nobody else gets to hear, a shared obsession, the thrill of knowing each other completely. Joint money, loans, and investments go oddly well when you're honest about them. The trap: needing drama to feel alive, so calm stretches feel suspicious. The move: when life is quiet, go deep on purpose and start a shared project with real stakes rather than inventing a threat.",
    Sagittarius: "You two get lucky the farther you go from home. The cheap flight that turned into the best week of your lives, the class one of you almost skipped, the stranger abroad who changed your plans. You're happiest laughing too loud in a new city, arguing about big ideas over late dinners, planning the next escape before this one ends. Optimism is your real asset; when one of you believes, the door opens. The trap: chasing the next horizon so hard that home feels like a waiting room. The move: bring one ritual back from every trip and actually keep doing it.",
    Capricorn: "Your luck is earned, and it holds. You two are the couple who bought the modest place early, stayed patient, and ended up ahead of everyone who laughed. Joy between you looks quieter than people expect: a paid-off card, a finished goal, a long walk after a brutal week. You get happier with every year, which surprises the friends who called you serious. The trap: postponing enjoyment until some milestone that keeps moving. The move: set a real reward for the next goal you hit, book it in advance, and refuse to cancel it when work gets busy.",
    Aquarius: "Things go right for you two when you do it your own way. The unconventional living setup, the friend group that feels like family, the side project nobody understood until it worked. You're happiest in a room full of odd, brilliant people or deep in a shared obsession at 2 a.m. Your best breaks come out of nowhere, usually through community. The trap: rejecting a good thing just because it looks too normal, like the ordinary holiday or the stable offer. The move: next time one of you says 'that's so basic,' try it anyway and notice whether you enjoy it.",
    Pisces: "Your luck as a couple feels slightly magical. The coincidence that saved the day, the song that played at exactly the right moment, the help that showed up when the money ran out. You two are happiest near water, lost in music, in a dark cinema holding hands, or doing something kind nobody sees. Giving comes back to you. The trap: waiting for the universe to fix practical problems, so bills pile up while you trust it'll work out. The move: pair every leap of faith with one boring action, the budget, the email, the appointment, and let the magic land on something solid.",
  },
  Vertex: {
    Aries: "The day you two met had a jolt to it, a collision rather than a slow approach. One of you made the first move so boldly the other still tells the story. Since then, the turning points in your relationship arrive fast: an ultimatum, a spontaneous move, a decision made in one heated night. You don't drift into new chapters; you crash into them. The trap: treating every fork in the road like an emergency and deciding before you've both caught your breath. The move: when life throws the next big choice at you, agree on a 48-hour pause before either of you commits.",
    Taurus: "Your meeting didn't feel dramatic at first. It felt like recognition, a steady click that neither of you could shake. The turning points between you are about what you build and keep: the first shared lease, the joint account, the moment one of you said 'I'm not going anywhere.' You two get bound by slow, physical commitments. Outsiders underestimate how fated you feel because it all looks so calm. The trap: resisting the next chapter because the current one is comfortable. The move: when life offers you a bigger step, treat your hesitation as a reason to look closer, not a reason to refuse.",
    Gemini: "You two were bound by a conversation. A message that shouldn't have been sent, a chat in a doorway that ran two hours, a mix-up that put you in the same place at the same time. Words keep being your turning points: the text that changed everything, the sentence overheard, the confession typed and deleted three times before sending. Your story has more coincidences than feels believable. The trap: talking your way around the big decision until the moment passes. The move: when a conversation starts to feel like a crossroads, one of you says 'this matters' and you both stay in it until it lands.",
    Cancer: "Meeting felt like coming home, like you'd already sat at each other's kitchen table. One of you felt instantly safe with the other, which was confusing given how guarded you both are. The turning points between you are domestic and emotional: moving in, a pregnancy scare or a real one, losing a parent, the holiday one of you was finally invited to. Each one binds you tighter. The trap: letting old family patterns decide the big moments instead of choosing them yourselves. The move: at every major crossroads, ask each other, 'Is this what we want, or what our families would do?'",
    Leo: "The moment you two met had an audience, or felt like it did: a party, a stage, a wedding, a room that went quiet. There was a spark of being chosen, and neither of you forgot it. Your turning points are big, visible, and romantic: the public declaration, the proposal, the risky creative leap one of you took because the other believed. You're bound by moments that felt like scenes from a film. The trap: waiting for the grand gesture while everyday choices quietly decide your future. The move: treat the small crossroads, the weeknight decisions, with the same seriousness you give the dramatic ones.",
    Virgo: "You two met through something ordinary: work, a gym, a clinic, a volunteer shift, a practical errand that turned into a life. Nothing about it looked fated until later. Your turning points arrive disguised as chores: a health scare one of you handled, a job change, the day one of you quietly started taking care of the other. Service binds you. The trap: dismissing the meaningful moments because they don't look romantic enough, then wondering where the magic went. The move: keep a running list of the small days that changed your direction, and read it out loud on your anniversary.",
    Libra: "Your meeting had a sense of rightness, like being introduced by someone who knew exactly what they were doing: a setup, a wedding, a mutual friend who insisted. From that first day you two looked like a pair before you were one. Your turning points involve other people: a rival, a third wheel, a friend's breakup that made you choose each other, the agreements that made it official. The trap: letting outside opinion decide the big steps, waiting for approval you don't need. The move: before announcing any major decision, settle it privately first and let no one else vote.",
    Scorpio: "Meeting each other felt dangerous in a good way. Something taboo, badly timed, or intense: one of you was with someone else, grieving, or in the middle of a collapse. You two got bound through crisis, and your turning points still arrive that way: a betrayal survived, a loss shared, a secret revealed that should have ended it and didn't. Each one strips something away and leaves you more tangled. The trap: believing your bond only proves itself through pain. The move: mark a turning point that comes from joy, a choice made because life is good, and give it equal weight.",
    Sagittarius: "You two met far from your usual lives: traveling, at school, on a detour, at a time when one of you was searching for something bigger. It felt like the world arranged it. Your turning points involve distance and belief: a long-distance stretch, a move across the country, a shared question about faith, the day you decided this relationship was an adventure worth betting on. The trap: running toward the next horizon whenever the present gets hard, and calling escape destiny. The move: when the urge to leap hits, ask each other whether you're growing or fleeing, and answer honestly before you book anything.",
    Capricorn: "Your meeting had weight from the start, as if you both knew it would cost something. The timing was strange: one of you older, busier, committed elsewhere, or at a hard career moment. You two get bound through responsibility, and your turning points look like adult decisions: the mortgage, the business, caring for a parent, choosing each other over an easier path. The relationship matured you both faster. The trap: treating the bond like a duty until tenderness gets scheduled out. The move: at every serious crossroads, add one thing that's purely for pleasure, so what you build together still feels like love.",
    Aquarius: "You two met in a way that makes people say 'that's so random.' An app glitch, a protest, a group chat, a wrong address, a friendship that flipped overnight. Nothing about your beginning followed the normal script, and neither do your turning points: sudden moves, unexpected job changes, the day you redefined what this relationship even is. Shocks bind you instead of breaking you. The trap: waiting for lightning and ignoring the steady choices that keep you together. The move: when life turns upside down again, name one thing between you that stays exactly the same, and protect it.",
    Pisces: "Your meeting felt like a dream you'd had before. A song, a strange coincidence, a night so hazy neither of you remembers who spoke first. You two were bound by something that felt spiritual, and your turning points keep arriving that way: a sacrifice one of you made, a rescue during a dark season, a synchronicity too strange to ignore. The trap: reading omens so hard that you avoid real conversations about what you want. The move: when something feels fated, write down what it's actually asking you to do, in plain words, and do that part together.",
  },
};

