    friction: "Needing closeness and needing space clash between you two. One of you wants routine; the other gets restless and pulls away the moment things get cozy. Moods swing without warning, and the steadier one keeps getting blindsided. The trap: one chases, one bolts, and you repeat the loop for months. The move: whoever needs space says exactly when they'll be back, and whoever needs closeness trusts that time.",
