    friction: "What makes you feel safe and what makes you feel loved don't line up. One of you wants to be taken out and treated; the other wants to stay in and be held. Money for comfort versus money for pleasure becomes a quiet recurring fight. The trap: feeling unloved because love arrived in the wrong form. The move: each of you names one small, specific thing that makes you feel cared for, and the other does it without being reminded.",
    fusion: "You two are soft together, maybe too soft. Affection, good food, long cuddles, and a beautiful home are the glue, and friends say your place is the coziest they know. Comfort spending creeps up, and conflict feels almost unbearable. The trap: using sweetness to dodge anything hard, until a small issue grows into a big one. The move: agree that one uncomfortable topic a week gets raised over a meal, and neither of you leaves the table.",
