    friction: "The relationship wants stability and one of you keeps shaking it, or you take turns. Plans change last minute, someone disappears into a new obsession, and the other feels left behind. The fights sound like 'you never commit' against 'you're suffocating me.' The trap: treating every surprise as betrayal, or every request as a cage. The move: agree on the three things that never change without warning, and let everything else stay loose.",
    fusion: "Nothing about you two stays still. You met in an unusual way, you break the rules other couples follow, and you reinvent the relationship every few years. It's exciting, and it's exhausting. Friends never know which version of you they'll get next. The trap: craving change so badly that you blow up something good just to feel alive again. The move: before any big shake-up, wait thirty days and check whether you both still want it.",
